\par\par \b \uc2 Turkey - Factors to Watch on Nov. 6\b0\par\par\uc2 481 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2020\par 05:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ANKARA, Nov 6 (Reuters) - Here are news, reports and events that may affect Turkish financial markets on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The lira stood at 8.4220 against the dollar at 0446 GMT, weakening from a close of 8.4135 on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The main BIST 100 share index rose 1.06% to 1,180.02 on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS\par \par \uc2 A gauge of Asian shares rallied to a near three-year peak while the dollar stayed sluggish and U.S. bond yields slipped on Friday in anticipation that a divided U.S. legislature would limit major policy changes and keep the status quo on economic policies.\par \par \uc2 Investors expect Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to beat President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the Republicans to retain control of the Senate, allowing them to block the Democrats' agenda, such as corporate tax hikes and massive borrowing for large spending.\par \par \uc2 ERDOGAN\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  will meet Sefik Dzaferovic, a Muslim Bosniak member of Bosnia's tripartite inter-ethnic presidency, in Istanbul (1130 GMT).\par \par \uc2 FOREIGN MINISTER\par \par \uc2 Foreign Minister Mevlut Cavusoglu will speak at a meeting of the South East European Cooperation Process (0800 GMT). He will later hold a news conference (1100 GMT).\par \par \uc2 CASH BALANCE\par \par \uc2 Turkish Treasury will announce October cash balance data.\par \par \uc2 ALBAYRAK ON LIRA\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister \uc2 Berat Albayrak\uc2  ruled out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the record-low lira \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reiterated government concerns that raising interest rates could hurt the economy, Milliyet newspaper reported on Thursday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent $101 billion to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets so far this year, \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  estimated on Thursday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  HOLDINGS\par \par \uc2 Turkish locals' holdings of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gold rose to a record high of $221.04 billion in the week to Oct. 30, extending a trend of dollarisation as the lira tumbled, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 TURKISH AIRLINES\par \par \uc2 Turkish Airlines\uc2 ' recent agreement with \uc2 Airbus\uc2  to delay the delivery of new aircraft means the company will postpone raising $5 billion of financing until after 2024, the airline's CFO said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 BLACK SEA DRILLING\par \par \uc2 Turkey began drilling at a second borehole in a Black Sea natural gas field where it made its largest ever discovery earlier this year, Energy Minister \uc2 Fatih Donmez\uc2  said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 CORONAVIRUS\par \par \uc2 Turkey identified 2,311 new symptomatic cases of coronavirus in the last 24 hours, data from the Health Ministry showed on Thursday. The total number of patients increased to 386,820 and the death toll increased by 81 to 10,639.\par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on:\par \par \uc2 Turkish politics <TR-POL>\par \par \uc2 Turkish equities <TR-E>\par \par \uc2 Turkish money <TR-M>\par \par \uc2 Turkish debt <TR-D>\par \par \uc2 Turkish hot stocks <TR-HOT>\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  news\par \par \uc2 All emerging market news\par \par \uc2 All Turkish news\par \par \uc2 For real-time quotes, double click on:\par \par \uc2 Istanbul National-100 stock index, interbank lira trading, lira bond trading (Writing by Ece Toksabay) \par \par \uc2 R