\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Turkish minister says no plans to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in lira -media\b0\par\par\uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2020\par 18:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (adds graphic)\par \par \uc2 By Ece Toksabay and Jonathan Spicer\par \par \uc2 ANKARA, Nov 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister \uc2 Berat Albayrak\uc2  ruled out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the record-low lira \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reiterated government concerns that raising interest rates could hurt the economy, Milliyet newspaper reported on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Albayrak said uncertainty around the U.S. election and the coronavirus pandemic had boosted the dollar, adding that the exchange rate was not the only factor reflecting Turkey's economic performance with production, exports and employment ahead of other countries, the newspaper said.\par \par \uc2 His comments coincided with data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showing net reserves have shrunk by $2.28 billion to $18.93 billion while Turkish locals' holdings of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gold - seen as a gauge of domestic confidence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - have risen to a record high of $221.04 billion.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the lira struggled again, hovering close to Tuesday's record low against the dollar - an outlier among emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  which enjoyed broad support as the greenback slipped to a two week low. The lira also briefly crashed through the 10 to the euro level, weakening nearly 1%.\par \par \uc2 Analysts increasingly expect that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , under pressure from stretched \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, could be forced to raise rates again to head off the lira's 30% depreciation this year, and to address inflation stuck around 12%. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tumbled more than 8% in just under two weeks.\par \par \uc2 Sticking to a familiar government line, Albayrak said it was possible to curb the rise of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  through interest rates but the government did not prefer this method because of "concern that a rate hike will decrease production and ... employment".\par \par \uc2 In the comments made in response to AK Party lawmakers Albayrak also added "the (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) fluctuation was not well above expectation" and an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange rate had not been considered yet.\par \par \uc2 Analysts are concerned about the toll of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on already stretched reserves, with \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  estimating on Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has burnt through $101 billion on such \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Albayrak's words did little to sooth investor concerns about the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's independence. Commerzbank analyst Tatha Ghose said the comments contradicted a tightening bias articulated by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CBT) and further undercut its political independence.\par \par \uc2 After a formal tightening in September, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held its policy rate steady at 10.25% last month, against expectations for a rate hike, but raised the top limit of its rate corridor to 14.07%.\par \par \uc2 So-called back-door measures had lifted the average cost of funding to 13.94% by Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "Albayrak basically confirmed that the CBT has gone out on a limb, without the blessing of political leaders, to tighten monetary policy" in recent months, Ghose said.\par \par \uc2 "The market will look through such tightening even more now, and the exchange rate is likely to soon come under pressure."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Ece Toksabay and Jonathan Spicer; additonal reporting by Karin Strohecker; Editing by Dominic Evans, Kirsten Donovan) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-11-5T18:21:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201105egb5017o9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
