\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Turkey mounts new defence of lira as locals snap up dollars\b0\par\par\uc2 709 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2020\par 18:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Interbank rate edges higher on Friday\par \par \uc2 * Analysts say more policy tightening on the cards\par \par \uc2 * Locals' \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings surge to $213 bln (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings, reserves, S&P, Erdogan)\par \par \uc2 By Nevzat Devranoglu, Orhan Coskun and Ebru Tuncay\par \par \uc2 ANKARA/ISTANBUL, Aug 7 (Reuters) - \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  squeezed some credit channels and signalled on Friday it would do more backdoor policy tightening to arrest a record drop in the lira, as data showed Turks snapped up more foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  than ever before.\par \par \uc2 Two weeks of volatile selling has left Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down nearly 20% against the dollar this year, among the worst performers in emerging markets, and exposed the limits of Ankara's costly \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 Ratings agencies told Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  may well have to formally tighten monetary policy - despite political opposition - to head off bigger economic problems, especially after locals added $9 billion in hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in two weeks.\par \par \uc2 Policies adopted after Turkey's 2018 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis "are reaching their limits and going forward it may be increasingly difficult to avoid a rate hike," said Maxim Rybnikov, associate director for EMEA sovereigns at S&P Global Ratings.\par \par \uc2 "If domestic Turkish residents lose faith, starting to increasingly convert to \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 , this can also precipitate a balance-of-payments stress," he said in an interview.\par \par \uc2 The lira fell 2.4% on Thursday and slid another 1.9% to an all time intraday low of 7.365 versus the dollar on Friday before bouncing back.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has turned to backdoor policy levers and in recent days lifted average funding costs from low levels, while the interbank rate also edged higher on Friday. It has also halted repo auctions and told lenders to use a 9.75% overnight rate instead.\par \par \uc2 BACKDOORS\par \par \uc2 However a formal policy tightening may be some way off after an aggressive year-long easing cycle bought the benchmark rate to 8.25%.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 , who opposes high rates and sacked the last \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief for ignoring instructions, said Friday the volatility is temporary and the economy's main problem is fallout from the coronavirus pandemic. His vice president said Turkey will overcome the "interest rate lobby" and \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  "manipulation".\par \par \uc2 After a meeting with \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Murat Uysal\uc2  late on Thursday, bank executives came away with the impression that planned policy steps will lift backdoor rates to stabilise things, even if the lira remains volatile, six sources told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 At the three-hour meeting, which included regulators, the bank clearly said funding costs will be increased but did not give a number, said the sources familiar with the call.\par \par \uc2 Bankers predicted backdoor tools to be used to effectively tighten policy by up to 300 basis points, and that there would be flexibility on asset ratio requirements. The average funding rate was 7.88%, up from 7.34% in mid-July after it cut sharply to limit coronavirus fallout.\par \par \uc2 "After the steps taken the lira's loss in value may continue for a while longer, but these steps in the medium term will play a very important role in achieving stability," said one banker, adding that the call was "positive".\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on the call.\par \par \uc2 FOREIGN \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  SURGE\par \par \uc2 Raising the stakes for Turkey, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held by locals swelled to $213 billion at the end of July, continuing a trend of dollarization, official data showed.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data also showed its \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  buffer declined in the last week with gross reserves down by nearly half so far this year at $47 billion, it lowest in years.\par \par \uc2 Data and traders' calculations show the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and state banks have sold some $110 billion since last year to underpin the lira. \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have picked up in recent weeks though it was uncertain whether the lira's recent drop reflected a policy change, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Analysts have said Turkey is running out of options to address low reserves and persistently high inflation and imports.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Tom Arnold in London, and Ezgi Erkoyun and Ali Kucukgocmen in Istanbul Writing by Jonathan Spicer Editing by Daren Butler, David Clarke and Frances Kerry) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-8-7T17:12:14.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200807eg87010jf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
