\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Russia lags EMEA on weak oil prices;  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 's lira rises\b0\par\par\uc2 490 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2020\par 13:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Lira likely supported by state bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Russian assets under pressure from weak oil\par \par \uc2 * CEE assets slightly higher as manufacturing improves (Recasts, adds details on Turkey, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Ambar Warrick\par \par \uc2 Aug 4 (Reuters) - Russian stocks and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were laggards in Europe, the Middle East and Africa (EMEA) on Tuesday due to weak oil prices, while most other regional markets gained on the back of improving U.S. economic data.\par \par \uc2 The rouble fell about 1% to the dollar, while stocks were weighed down by losses in major energy firms.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices retreated amid concerns that a fresh wave of COVID-19 infections will see a global demand recovery stalling due to tighter lockdowns.\par \par \uc2 However, positive U.S. manufacturing data helped lift broader sentiment, with markets also keeping a close watch on talks over fresh stimulus measures in the world's largest economy.\par \par \uc2 The Turkish lira rose as much as 0.7% to the dollar, as the interest rate on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overnight swap transactions in the London market surged to 520%.\par \par \uc2 Turkish banks have previously cut funding to the London swap market, effectively making it impossible to short the lira in order to curb falls in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "State banks have been reportedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , trying to slow down the pace of lira depreciation," said \uc2 Piotr Matys\uc2 , Emerging Markets \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategist at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Such a move is the indication of the ongoing negative sentiment against the lira."\par \par \uc2 Data showed Turkey's July manufacturing activity grew at its fastest pace in nine years, while moderating consumer price inflation in the country pointed to more economic stability. However, analysts were sceptical that inflation could remain fettered.\par \par \uc2 Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Hungarian forint and the Polish zloty moved in a flat-to-high range against the euro.\par \par \uc2 Polish manufacturing recovered in July after the easing of coronavirus-led restrictions, a survey showed on Monday, but Hungary posted a more modest improvement and the Czech Republic did not return to growth.\par \par \uc2 Emerging market risk assets had marked strong gains in July, amid improving economic data and hopes for a coronavirus vaccine. But they are yet to reach pre-pandemic levels.\par \par \uc2 In Latin America, Argentina said it had reached a deal with three creditor groups to restructure $65 billion in sovereign debt, which would help it climb out of a damaging default and revive an economy stuck in recession for over two years.\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  performance in 2020, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh}}}\uc2  For GRAPHIC on MSCI emerging index performance in 2020, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/2OusNdX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/2OusNdX}}}\par \par \uc2 For TOP NEWS across emerging markets\par \par \uc2 For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par \uc2 For TURKISH market report, see\par \par \uc2 For RUSSIAN market report, see (Reporting by Ambar Warrick in Bengaluru; Editing by Ramakrishnan M. and Anil D'Silva) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-8-4T12:13:56.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200804eg84020rh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
