\par\par \b \uc2 Turkey - Factors to Watch on June 22\b0\par\par\uc2 495 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2020\par 07:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ANKARA, June 22 (Reuters) - Here are news, reports and events that may affect Turkish financial markets on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The lira stood at 6.8400 against the U.S. dollar at 0500 GMT, marginally firmer than Friday's close of 6.8430.\par \par \uc2 The main BIST 100 share index rose 0.99% to 113,611.89 on Friday.\par \par \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS\par \par \uc2 U.S. stock futures erased losses and Asian stocks held flat on Monday, trying to shake off worries that rising coronavirus cases in the United States could scupper a quick economic rebound from the massive downturn triggered by the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 CORONAVIRUS\par \par \uc2 The number of people who have died from COVID-19 in Turkey rose on Sunday by 23 to 4,950, Health Ministry data showed. The overall number of cases rose by 1,192 to 187,685, the data showed, with 160,240 recovered from the virus.\par \par \uc2 On Saturday, President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  said Turkey had lost some ground in its battle with the coronavirus but a focus on hygiene, masks and social distancing will protect people and help the economy rebound in the second half of the year.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspended until year end a requirement that banks with a real annual loan growth rate above 15% must keep their adjusted rate below 15%, so they can keep credit flowing as the economy reopens from a coronavirus lockdown.\par \par \uc2 MILITARY \b \highlight22\uc2 OPERATION\b0 \highlight\uc2  IN NORTHERN IRAQ\par \par \uc2 One Turkish soldier was killed on Sunday during Turkey's military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Northern Iraq targeting Kurdish militants, Turkish defence ministry said. Two Kurdish militants were killed in the same \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ministry added.\par \par \uc2 TRADE MINISTER\par \par \uc2 Trade Minister Ruhsah Pekcan will attend the opening ceremony of a virtual fair of agriculture and animal husbandry machinery (0800 GMT).\par \par \uc2 FLOOD IN WESTERN TURKEY\par \par \uc2 At least four people in Bursa province in northwestern Turkey have died in floods caused by heavy rains, officials said on Monday. Search and rescue \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  are underway to find at least two people still missing, the local governor said.\par \par \uc2 LIBYA\par \par \uc2 Egypt's President \uc2 Abdel Fattah\uc2  al-Sisi on Saturday said his country has a legitimate right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in neighbouring Libya and ordered his army to be ready to carry out any mission outside the country, if necessary.\par \par \uc2 Sisi's comments came amid high tensions over regional rival \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Libya. He also warned forces loyal to the internationally recognised Government of National Accord (GNA) in Tripoli not to cross the current frontline with \uc2 Khalifa Haftar\uc2 's eastern-based Libyan National Army (LNA). \par \par \uc2 \f2               \par               \par               \par               \par For other related news, double click on:\par               \par Turkish politics <TR-POL>\par               \par Turkish equities <TR-E>\par               \par Turkish money <TR-M>\par               \par Turkish debt <TR-D>\par               \par Turkish hot stocks <TR-HOT>\par               \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par               \par All emerging market news\par               \par All Turkish news\par               \par For real-time quotes, double click on:\par          