\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-\uc2 Turkish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  says used Chinese yuan funding for first time\b0\par\par\uc2 232 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2020\par 15:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds background on \uc2 Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves)\par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, June 19 (Reuters) - \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it had used a funding facility for Chinese yuan for the first time under a prior swap agreement with the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the transaction on Thursday, Turkish companies in various sectors paid, via banks, their import bills from China using yuan, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 It added that the move would strengthen cooperation between Turkey and China, and that commercial banks would be able to add products related to trade and financial activities with a strategy based on the swap agreement.\par \par \uc2 A fall in the \uc2 Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, partly caused by state bank \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the lira, has raised concerns that \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  would need foreign funding.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reported in May that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was making efforts to establish swap lines with the central banks of England and Japan and expand its existing swap lines with Qatar and China.\par \par \uc2 The tripling of the swap line with Qatar to $15 billion equivalent in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month led to an $8 billion rise in the reserves, but analysts said it was far from meeting the country's needs.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Ali Kucukgocmen; editing by Jonathan Spicer, Larry King) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-6-19T14:53:16.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200619eg6j024md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
