\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Qatar offers Turkey relief by tripling  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  swap line to $15 bln\b0\par\par\uc2 492 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 2020\par 15:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Turkey seeking foreign funding to boost reserves, lira\par \par \uc2 * Ankara also appealed to Beijing, London, Tokyo for swaps\par \par \uc2 * Senior official tells Reuters talks continuing (Adds analyst comment)\par \par \uc2 By Ali Kucukgocmen and Orhan Coskun\par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, May 20 (Reuters) - Turkey secured a tripling of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -swap agreement with Qatar to $15 billion, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday, providing much-needed foreign funding to reinforce its depleted reserves and help steady the Turkish lira.\par \par \uc2 Ankara had been urgently seeking access to funds from Doha and elsewhere to head off a potential \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spiral, and analysts say tens of billions of dollars might be needed. A senior Turkish official told Reuters talks are continuing.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the deal with its Qatari counterpart - which raised the existing \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  limit from the equivalent of $5 billion - would support financial stability and trade.\par \par \uc2 The lira touched a historic low earlier this month as investors fretted over a drop in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's net \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3bOJYmo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/3bOJYmo}}}\uc2  and Turkey's relatively high foreign debt obligations, accelerating Ankara's overseas funding search.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reported last week that officials from Turkey's Treasury and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had appealed to counterparts in Qatar and China about expanding existing swap lines, and to the United Kingdom and Japan about possibly establishing them.\par \par \uc2 Turkey has a roughly $1.7 billion swap facility with Beijing.\par \par \uc2 "Talks on swaps are continuing and especially some are in a very positive situation. We expect positive results from them soon as well," the senior Turkish official said before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement.\par \par \uc2 The official, who requested anonymity, characterized some of the conversations as ongoing and others as on hold.\par \par \uc2 The lira has rallied over the last eight trading days on expectations of new funding. Some analysts said the volatility and a 14% drop so far this year risked escalating as in 2018, when Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis shook emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 The lira was 0.1% weaker at 6.7900 versus the dollar at 1317 GMT.\par \par \uc2 "The extra $10 billion is a drop in the ocean compared to Turkey's external funding needs," especially given hard-hit tourism and trade have widened the current account deficit, said \uc2 Jason Tuvey\uc2 , senior economist at Capital Economics.\par \par \uc2 "We could see pressure on the lira start to mount again" if the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  and \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  rebuff Turkey, he said.\par \par \uc2 Net \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have fallen to $26 billion from $40 billion this year, in part due to state bank \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help stabilize the lira, analysts say. \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 12-month foreign debt obligations are $168 billion.\par \par \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  analysts said the boost from Qatar "only closes roughly a third of the funding gap we see for 2020."\par \par \uc2 (Writing by Jonathan Spicer; Editing by Dominic Evans/Mark Heinrich) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-5-20T14:30:23.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200520eg5k00z9j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw94\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1410\pichgoal600
