\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Turkish lira steadies a day after touching record low\b0\par\par\uc2 409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2020\par 10:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds comment, context on cash crunch; updates prices)\par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, May 8 (Reuters) - The Turkish lira was steady on Friday after rebounding from a record low the day before, but concerns loomed over the country's depleted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3bOJYmo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/3bOJYmo}}}\uc2  and foreign financing needs as the coronavirus pandemic slows economic activity.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood at 7.1075 at 0831 GMT, weakening slightly from a close of 7.1000 on Thursday, when it hit an all-time low of 7.2690 during the trading day.\par \par \uc2 The lira has lost some 18% this year under pressure from the novel coronavirus, which has killed more than 3,600 people in Turkey. It has weakened despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  funding of state banks' \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts say.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strategy of spending billions of dollars to prop up the lira is not working as reflected in the precipitous rise of USD/TRY to a new all-time high," said \uc2 Piotr Matys\uc2 , senior emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Turkish officials continue to argue that hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buffers are sufficient. The market has the opposite view on this crucial issue," he added.\par \par \uc2 The lira and some other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were in part lifted by signs of an improvement in frayed Sino-U.S. relations.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Turkey's banking watchdog blocked \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 , Citibank and \uc2 UBS\uc2  from making lira transactions, saying they were unable to fulfil lira liabilities in due time.\par \par \uc2 Adding to state pressure on banks, government-owned Anadolu news agency had reported the watchdog was launching legal action against London-based institutions it said had mounted a "manipulative attack" on the lira.\par \par \uc2 Turkey has asked the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and other central banks for access to funds as its own net foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have fallen to around $28 billion from $40 billion so far this year, reaching as low as $25 billion two weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's Finance Minister \uc2 Berat Albayrak\uc2  voiced optimism in a conference call with investors on Wednesday about sealing a swap line deal for \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  funding, several participants in the call told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 However, comments by a \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  policymaker late on Wednesday have been interpreted by traders as ruling out a Fed swap line to cushion Ankara's depleted reserves.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Daren Butler; Editing by Amy Caren Daniel and Jonathan Spicer) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-5-8T09:58:08.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200508eg5801awx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
