nd do not address the \par suitability of any security. S&P assumes no obligation to update the Content \par following publication in any form or format.  The Content should not be relied \par on and is not a substitute for the skill, judgment, and experience of the \par user, its management, employees, advisors, and/or clients when making \par investment and other business decisions. S&P does not act as a fiduciary or \par an investment advisor except where registered as such. While S&P has obtained \par information from sources it believes to be reliable, S&P does not perform an \par audit and undertakes no duty of due diligence or independent verification of \par any information it receives. \par  \par To the extent that regulatory authorities allow a rating agency to acknowledge \par in one jurisdiction a rating issued in another jurisdiction for certain \par regulatory purposes, S&P reserves the right to assign, withdraw, or suspend \par such acknowledgement at any time and in its sole discretion. S&P Parties \par disclaim any duty whatsoever arising out of the assignment, withdrawal, or \par suspension of an acknowledgment as well as any liability for any damage \par alleged to have been suffered on account thereof. \par  \par S&P keeps certain activities of its business units separate from each other in \par order to preserve the independence and objectivity of their respective \par activities. As a result, certain business units of S&P may have information \par that is not available to other S&P business units. S&P has established \par policies and procedures to maintain the confidentiality of certain nonpublic \par information received in connection with each analytical process. \par  \par S&P may receive compensation for its ratings and certain analyses, normally \par from issuers or underwriters of securities or from obligors. S&P reserves the \par right to disseminate its opinions and analyses. S&P's public ratings and \par analyses are made available on