\par\par \b \uc2 Turkish lira weakens slightly after Iran strikes\b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2020\par 08:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Jan 8 (Reuters) - The Turkish lira weakened slightly on Wednesday, remaining around its weakest levels in seven months, after Iran fired missiles at U.S.-led forces in Iraq.\par \par \uc2 The lira stood at 5.9755 against the dollar at 0730 GMT, compared with a close on Tuesday of 5.9730 and having weakened as far as 5.9885 overnight after initial news of the missile strikes emerged.\par \par \uc2 "We expected very strong global selling pressure, but the lira reaction was virtually non-existent," a treasury desk trader at one bank said, pointing to a modest change in oil prices as one reason for the limited \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  move.\par \par \uc2 Iranian state television said Iran had fired 15 missiles at U.S. targets in Iraq early on Wednesday. The U.S. military said at least two Iraqi facilities hosting U.S.-led coalition personnel were targeted.\par \par \uc2 "Investors will now focus on how the United States plans to respond. Turkey may be affected more by the atmosphere of rising tension due to its proximity to the region and its hosting of U.S. bases," the trader said.\par \par \uc2 The Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened 11% last year, in part due to Turkey's military incursion in Syria and the threat of U.S. sanctions, bringing losses over the last two years to 36%.\par \par \uc2 Traders said on Monday that state banks had been selling dollars to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through market turbulence after last week's U.S. killing of a top Iranian commander, which triggered the Iranian retaliation.\par \par \uc2 State banks have not spoken publicly about the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said they have been more active in markets this year conducting two-way transactions.\par \par \uc2 The yield on the benchmark 10-year bond, which has fallen from 21% in May, was steady at 12.28% on Wednesday. The main BIST 100 share index was down 0.76%. (Reporting by Nevzat Devranoglu; Writing by Daren Butler; Editing by Dominic Evans) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-1-8T08:51:47.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200108eg18015o1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
