\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-State banks help steady Turkish lira despite oil jump\b0\par\par\uc2 534 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2020\par 11:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds oil price, comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , byline)\par \par \uc2 By Nevzat Devranoglu\par \par \uc2 ANKARA, Jan 6 (Reuters) - The Turkish lira was flat on Monday despite another jump in oil prices, and three traders said state banks were again selling dollars to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through market turbulence after the U.S. killing of a top Iranian commander.\par \par \uc2 The lira was at 5.9735 against the dollar, little changed from Friday's close at 5.9740.\par \par \uc2 It weakened 11% last year, in part due to Turkey's military incursion in Syria and the threat of U.S. sanctions, bringing losses over the last two years to 36%.\par \par \uc2 "The state (banks) are in the market on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply side today too, as they were on Friday," one trader said. "It is difficult to say how many dollars are being sold but it's clear they will not allow an excessive loss in the lira's value."\par \par \uc2 Since March of last year, traders have pointed to occasional state bank \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilize the lira.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. killing last week of Iranian commander \uc2 Qassem Soleimani\uc2  fuelled geopolitical tensions and brought more selling pressure on both the lira and on oil, sending crude prices up another 2% on Monday and hurting emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Turkey relies on imports for almost all of its energy consumption including oil.\par \par \uc2 State banks have not spoken publicly about the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said they have been more active in markets this year conducting two-way transactions.\par \par \uc2 "We can say that there was support for the lira, particularly on Friday, in order to reduce the impact of geopolitical tension," said a senior banker.\par \par \uc2 "When we look at state banks' \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions, we can see that in the last weeks of the year steps began to support the lira."\par \par \uc2 The yield on the benchmark 10-year bond, which has fallen from 21% in May, was steady at 12.4% on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The main BIST 100 share index, which fell 1.94% on Friday, was down 1.4% on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Investors are also weighing up the outlook for Turkish monetary policy after data on Friday showed annual inflation rose slightly more than expected to 11.84% in December, narrowing the window for more rate cuts in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Encouraged by the government to cut aggressively to lift the economy out of recession, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slashed its key policy rate to 12% by December from 24% in July.\par \par \uc2 Bankers said the Treasury could make a eurobond issue this week but such an issue, often made early in the year, could be delayed for several weeks due to the lessened global appetite.\par \par \uc2 The Treasury will begin switch auctions this week, holding three such auctions on Tuesday. It will buy back fixed-coupon, floating-rate and CPI-indexed securities maturing in 2020 and issue bonds maturing in 2027.\par \par \uc2 Investors who met Turkish authorities in September told Reuters they expected the Treasury to start issuing longer-term bonds after the sharp cuts in interest rates. (Additional reporting by Jonathan Spicer; Writing by Daren Butler; Editing by Dominic Evans) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-1-6T11:50:45.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200106eg1601bgd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
