\par\par \b \uc2 *\uc2 Fitch\uc2  Downgrades 14 Turkish Banks; Outlook Negative\b0\par\par\uc2 3,368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2019\par 15:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2019, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 19 Jul 2019 09:00 ET  Press Release: \uc2 Fitch\uc2  Downgrades 14 Turkish Banks; Outlook Negative\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par The following is a press release from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2  : \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 - Link to \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2  ' Report(s): \uc2 Fitch\uc2  Downgrades 14 Turkish Banks; Outlook Negative\par \par \uc2 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fitchratings.com/site/re/10083250"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.fitchratings.com/site/re/10083250 }}}\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2  -London-19 July 2019: \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2  has downgraded the support-driven Long-Term Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Issuer Default Ratings (LTFC IDRs) of 12 foreign-owned Turkish banks and their subsidiaries, and two state-owned development banks, Turkiye Ihracat Kredi Bankasi A.S. (\uc2 Turk Eximbank\uc2  ) and Turkiye Kalkinma Bankasi A.S. (TKYB).\par \par \uc2 The agency has also downgraded the Long-Term Local \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDRs of 22 banks and their subsidiaries. The Outlooks on all banks' Long-Term IDRs are Negative. Viability Ratings (VRs) are not affected as a result of these rating actions. A full list of rating actions is available at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.fitchratings.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.fitchratings.com}}}\uc2  or via the link above.\par \par \uc2 The rating actions follow the downgrade of Turkey's sovereign rating on 12 July 2019 (see "\uc2 Fitch\uc2  Downgrades Turkey to 'BB-'; Outlook Negative" at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.fitchratings.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.fitchratings.com}}}\uc2 ). In \uc2 Fitch\uc2 's view, the dismissal of \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor heightens doubts about the authorities' tolerance for a period of sustained below-trend growth and disinflation that \uc2 Fitch\uc2  considers consistent with a rebalancing and stabilisation of the economy, and highlights a deterioration in Turkey's institutional independence and economic policy coherence and credibility.\par \par \uc2 The downgrades of the foreign-owned Turkish banks' LTFC IDRs to 'B+' from 'BB-' reflects increased risk of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the banking sector in case of a marked deterioration in Turkey's external finances. We continue to view the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that would prevent banks from servicing their FC obligations to be slightly higher than that of a sovereign default, and this result in these ratings being capped one notch below the sovereign LTFC IDR.\par \par \uc2 The one-notch downgrades of the support-driven LTFC IDRs of state-owned development banks TKYB, to 'BB-', and \uc2 Turk Eximbank\uc2  , to 'B+', reflect \uc2 Fitch\uc2 's view of the increased risks to the ability of the Turkish authorities to provide timely and sufficient support in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  (FC) given the increased potential for stress in the country's external finances. \uc2 Turk Eximbank\uc2  is rated one notch below Turkey, while TKYB is equalised with the sovereign rating due to its small size and high, albeit reduced, proportion of Turkish treasury-guaranteed funding.\par \par \uc2 The VRs of all banks under review, and of other \uc2 Fitch\uc2 -rated Turkish banks, are unaffected following the sovereign downgrade. This reflects our view that VRs are already in the 'b' category and therefore capture higher systemic risk: the highest Turkish bank VRs of 'b+' are still one notch below the sovereign ratings.\par \par \uc2 KEY RATING DRIVERS\par \par \uc2 - IDRS, SUPPORT RATINGS AND SENIOR DEBT RATINGS OF FOREIGN-OWNED BANKS\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Turkiye Garanti Bankasi A.S \uc2 . (Garanti \uc2 BBVA\uc2 ; LTFC IDR B+/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Yapi ve Kredi Bankasi A.S \uc2 . (YKB; LTFC IDR B+/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Turk Ekonomi Bankasi\uc2  (TEB; LTFC IDR B+/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - QNB Finansbank A.S. (LTFC IDR B+/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - ING Bank A.S. (LTFC IDR B+/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Kuveyt Turk Katilim Bankasi\uc2  (Kuveyt Turk; LTFC IDR B+/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Alternatifbank A.S\uc2 . (\uc2 Alternatifbank\uc2  ; LTFC IDR B+/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - Turkiye Finans Katilim Bankasi (TFKB; LTFC IDR B+/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - Burgan Bank A.S. (Burgan Bank Turkey; LTFC IDR B+/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 ICBC Turkey Bank A.S \uc2 . (LTFC IDR B+/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - BankPozitif Kredi ve Kalkinma Bankasi (BankPozitif; LTFC IDR B+/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Denizbank A.S\uc2  . (LTFC IDR B+/Negative)\par \par \uc2 The foreign-owned banks' LTFC IDRs and FC senior debt ratings are downgraded by one notch to 'B+', one notch below the sovereign LTFC IDR. This reflects our view that in case of a marked deterioration in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's external finances, the risk of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the banking sector would be higher than that of a sovereign default.\par \par \uc2 In \uc2 Fitch\uc2 's view, Turkey's high external funding requirement creates a significant incentive to retain market access and avoid capital controls. Nevertheless, if there were a marked deterioration in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's external finances some form of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the banking system that might impede the banks' ability to service their FC obligations would become more likely, in \uc2 Fitch\uc2 's view.\par \par \uc2 Nine foreign-owned banks now have FC IDRs and FC senior debt ratings at the level of their VRs, but also underpinned by shareholder support. The FC IDRs of \uc2 Alternatifbank\uc2  , Burgan Bank Turkey and BankPozitif remain driven solely by shareholder support. \uc2 Fitch\uc2 's view of support for all foreign-owned banks is based on their strategic importance, to varying degrees, for their parents, integration, roles within their respective groups and, for some, common branding.\par \par \uc2 All foreign-owned banks' LT LC IDRs are also downgraded by one notch. Their LT LC IDRs are one notch above their LTFC IDRs, reflecting our view of a lower likelihood of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that would impede the banks' ability to service obligations in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 -\par \par \uc2 - IDRs, SUPPORT RATINGS AND SENIOR DEBT RATINGS OF STATE-OWNED COMMERCIAL BANKS AND DEVELOPMENT BANKS\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 T.C. Ziraat Bankasi A.S \uc2 . (Ziraat; LTFC IDR B+/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - Turkiye Halk Bankasi A.S. (Halk; LTFC IDR B+ /Negative)\par \par \uc2 - Turkiye Vakiflar Bankasi A.S. (\uc2 Vakifbank\uc2  ; LTFC IDR B+ /Negative)\par \par \uc2 - Vakif Katilim Bankasi A.S. (Vakif Katilim; LTFC IDR B+/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - Turkiye Sinai Kalkinma Bankasi A.S. (TSKB; LTFC IDR B+/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - Turkiye Ihracat Kredi Bankasi A.S. (\uc2 Turk Eximbank\uc2  ; LTFC IDR B+ /Negative)\par \par \uc2 - Turkiye Kalkinma ve Yatirim Bankasi A.S. (TKYB; LTFC IDR BB-/Negative)\par \par \uc2 TKYB's LTFC IDR has been downgraded by one notch to 'BB-' from 'BB'. The bank's ratings remain equalised with the sovereign, reflecting its small size and still largely treasury-guaranteed funding base.\par \par \uc2 Turk Eximbank\uc2  's LTFC IDR has also been downgraded by one notch, to 'B+' from 'BB-'. The bank's ratings reflect \uc2 Fitch\uc2 's view of the high propensity of the government to provide support given \uc2 Turk Eximbank\uc2  's ownership, policy role and high level of state-related funding. However, \uc2 Turk Eximbank\uc2  is rated one notch below the sovereign due to its larger (than TKYB) balance sheet and volumes of foreign funding and risks to the ability of the authorities to provide support in FC.\par \par \uc2 The Support Rating Floors (SRFs) of the state-owned commercial banks (Ziraat, \uc2 Vakifbank\uc2  , Halk, Vakif Katilim), and of privately owned development bank TSKB, have been affirmed at 'B+' despite the sovereign downgrade.\par \par \uc2 This reflects a degree of rating compression at lower rating levels, and also considers the high government propensity to support these banks given their majority state ownership (except for TSKB), systemic importance (Ziraat, \uc2 Vakifbank\uc2  , Halk), policy roles (Ziraat, Halk, TSKB), significant state-related funding, state guarantees in the case of TSKB, and the recent record of support. The one-notch difference between the sovereign rating and those of these banks reflects the limited ability of the authorities to provide support in FC.\par \par \uc2 The authorities have shown a strong commitment to support the state banks, as indicated by capital increases in September 2018 and April 2019.\par \par \uc2 The LTFC IDRs of Halk and Vakif Katilim have been affirmed following the affirmation of their SRFs, which drive their LTFC IDRs.\par \par \uc2 The LTLC IDRs of the state-owned commercial banks and the development banks have been downgraded to 'BB-' and are equalised with the sovereign rating, reflecting the stronger ability of the sovereign to provide support in LC.\par \par \uc2 The Negative Outlooks on the banks' Long-Term IDRs mirror those on the sovereign ratings. For Ziraat, \uc2 Vakifbank\uc2  and TSKB, which have VRs at the level of their SRFs, the Outlooks on the LTFC IDRs also reflect the potential for their VRs to be downgraded if there were further deterioration in the operating environment or increases in risk appetite that place greater-than-expected pressure on financial metrics (Ziraat and \uc2 Vakifbank\uc2  only) .\par \par \uc2 LONG-TERM LOCAL \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDRS AND SUPPORT RATING FLOORS OF AKBANK AND ISBANK\par \par \uc2 Akbank TAS\uc2  (LTFC IDR 'B+'/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Turkiye Is Bankasi\uc2  (LTFC IDR 'B+'/Negative)\par \par \uc2 The LTLC IDRs of Akbank and Isbank have been downgraded to 'B+' from 'BB-' and are now in line with their LTFC IDRs. The LTLC IDRs are underpinned by potential state support and the downgrades reflect the sovereign downgrade.\par \par \uc2 Both the banks' LTLC IDRs and LTFC IDRs are now in line with their VRs. The Negative Outlooks on their IDRs reflect the potential for further deterioration in the operating environment, which could place greater pressure on the banks' financial metrics.\par \par \uc2 -\par \par \uc2 - The affirmation of the 'B' SRFs of Akbank and Isbank, two notches below the sovereign LTFC IDR (at the level of the domestic systemically important bank (D-\uc2 SIB\uc2 ) SRF for Turkish banks), reflects their systemic importance, but also their private ownership and the Turkish authorities' limited ability to provide support in FC, if needed.\par \par \uc2 SUBORDINATED DEBT RATINGS\par \par \uc2 - The subordinated notes ratings of YKB, Kuveyt Turk, Garanti and \uc2 Alternatifbank\uc2  are notched down once from their IDRs and have been downgraded by one notch in line with the downgrades of their anchor ratings. The notching in each case includes one notch for loss severity and zero notches for non-performance risk (relative to the anchor ratings).\par \par \uc2 SUBSIDIARY RATINGS\par \par \uc2 Ak Yatirim (LTFC IDR 'B+' /Negative)\par \par \uc2 - Ak Finansal Kiralama (LTFC IDR 'B+' /Negative)\par \par \uc2 - Alternatif Finansal Kiralama AS (LTFC IDR 'B+'/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - Deniz Finansal Kiralama (LTFC IDR 'B+'/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - Joint-Stock Company Denizbank Moscow (LTFC IDR 'B+'/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Garanti Faktoring\uc2  (LTFC IDR 'B+'/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - Garanti Finansal Kiralama (LTFC IDR 'B+'/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Is Finansal Kiralama\uc2  (LTFC IDR 'B+'/Negative)\par \par \uc2 - QNB Finans Finansal Kiralama A.S. (LTFC IDR 'B+'/ Negative)\par \par \uc2 - Yapi Kredi Finansal Kiralama (LTFC IDR 'B+'/ Negative)\par \par \uc2 - Yapi Kredi Faktoring (LTFC IDR 'B+'/ Negative)\par \par \uc2 - Yapi Kredi Yatirim Menkul Degerler (LTFC IDR 'B+'/Negative)\par \par \uc2 19 Jul 2019 09:00 ET  Press Release: \uc2 Fitch\uc2  Downgrades 14 Turkish Banks; -2-\par \par \uc2 - Ziraat Katilim Bankasi (LTFC IDR 'B+' /Negative)\par \par \uc2 Subsidiary ratings are equalised with those of parent banks, reflecting their strategic importance to, and integration within, their respective groups. The downgrades of the LT IDRs of the subsidiaries of foreign-owned banks (\uc2 Alternatifbank\uc2  , \uc2 Denizbank\uc2 , Garanti, \uc2 QNB Finansbank\uc2  and YKB), and of the LTLC IDRs of the subsidiaries of Akbank, Isbank and Ziraat, mirror the rating actions on their respective parents.\par \par \uc2 RATING SENSITIVITIES\par \par \uc2 - FOREIGN-OWNED BANKS\par \par \uc2 - The LT IDRs, Support Ratings and senior debt ratings of foreign-owned banks could be downgraded if \uc2 Fitch\uc2  believes the risk of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the banking sector has increased materially. The Negative Outlooks on these banks reflect the potential for a further deterioration in Turkey's external finances, which could increase the risk of such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A sovereign downgrade would be likely to lead to downgrades of these banks.\par \par \uc2 STATE-OWNED COMMERCIAL AND DEVELOPMENT BANKS\par \par \uc2 - The IDRs and senior debt ratings of Ziraat, Halk, \uc2 Vakifbank\uc2  , Vakif Katilim, TSKB, \uc2 Turk Eximbank\uc2  and TKYB could be downgraded if \uc2 Fitch\uc2  concludes that the ability of the sovereign to provide support has weakened. However, the ratings of Ziraat, \uc2 Vakifbank\uc2  and TSKB would only be downgraded if their 'b+' VRs were also lowered.\par \par \uc2 AKBANK AND ISBANK\par \par \uc2 - The LTFC IDRs and senior debt ratings of Akbank and Isbank are sensitive to any changes to their VRs. The banks' LTLC IDRs are underpinned by state support at the 'B+' level, and so would only be downgraded if both our assessment of support weakened and the VRs were downgraded.\par \par \uc2 SUBORDINATED DEBT RATINGS\par \par \uc2 - Subordinated debt ratings are primarily sensitive to changes in banks' anchor ratings, namely the Long-Term IDRs for YKB, Garanti, Kuveyt Turk and \uc2 Alternatifbank\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 These ratings are also sensitive to a change in notching from the anchor ratings due to a revision in \uc2 Fitch\uc2 's assessment of the probability of the notes' non-performance risk or of loss severity in case of non-performance.\par \par \uc2 SUBSIDIARY RATINGS\par \par \uc2 - The ratings of these entities are sensitive to changes in the Long-Term IDRs of their parents.\par \par \uc2 -\par \par \uc2 - Contact:\par \par \uc2 - For the respective analytical contacts, see the associated Rating Action Report.\par \par \uc2 Committee Chairperson\par \par \uc2 - Mahin Dissanayake\par \par \uc2 - Senior Director\par \par \uc2 - +44 20 3530 1618\par \par \uc2 Media Relations: Louisa Williams, London, Tel: +44 20 3530 2452, Email: louisa.williams@thefitchgroup.com.\par \par \uc2 Additional information is available on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.fitchratings.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.fitchratings.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Applicable Criteria\par \par \uc2 - Bank Rating Criteria (pub. 12 Oct 2018)\par \par \uc2 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fitchratings.com/site/re/10044408"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.fitchratings.com/site/re/10044408 }}}\par \par \uc2 - Non-Bank Financial Institutions Rating Criteria (pub. 12 Oct 2018)\par \par \uc2 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fitchratings.com/site/re/10044407"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.fitchratings.com/site/re/10044407 }}}\par \par \uc2 - Short-Term Ratings Criteria (pub. 02 May 2019)\par \par \uc2 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fitchratings.com/site/re/10073011"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.fitchratings.com/site/re/10073011 }}}\par \par \uc2 Additional Disclosures\par \par \uc2 - Dodd-Frank Rating Information Disclosure Form\par \par \uc2 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fitchratings.com/site/dodd-frank-disclosure/10083196"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.fitchratings.com/site/dodd-frank-disclosure/10083196 }}}\par \par \uc2 - Solicitation Status\par \par \uc2 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fitchratings.com/site/pr/10083196#solicitation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.fitchratings.com/site/pr/10083196#solicitation }}}\par \par \uc2 - Endorsement Policy\par \par \uc2 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fitchratings.com/regulatory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.fitchratings.com/regulatory }}}\par \par \uc2 ALL FITCH CREDIT RATINGS ARE SUBJECT TO CERTAIN LIMITATIONS AND DISCLAIMERS. PLEASE READ THESE LIMITATIONS AND DISCLAIMERS BY FOLLOWING THIS LINK: HTTPS://WWW.FITCHRATINGS.COM/UNDERSTANDINGCREDITRATINGS. IN ADDITION, RATING DEFINITIONS AND THE TERMS OF USE OF SUCH RATINGS ARE AVAILABLE ON THE AGENCY'S PUBLIC WEB SITE AT WWW.FITCHRATINGS.COM. PUBLISHED RATINGS, CRITERIA, AND METHODOLOGIES ARE AVAILABLE FROM THIS SITE AT ALL TIMES. FITCH'S CODE OF CONDUCT, CONFIDENTIALITY, CONFLICTS OF INTEREST, AFFILIATE FIREWALL, COMPLIANCE, AND OTHER RELEVANT POLICIES AND PROCEDURES ARE ALSO AVAILABLE FROM THE CODE OF CONDUCT SECTION OF THIS SITE. DIRECTORS AND SHAREHOLDERS RELEVANT INTERESTS ARE AVAILABLE AT HTTPS://WWW.FITCHRATINGS.COM/SITE/REGULATORY. FITCH MAY HAVE PROVIDED ANOTHER PERMISSIBLE SERVICE TO THE RATED ENTITY OR ITS RE