\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Qatar promises to invest 15 billion dollars in Turkey. Lira recovers\b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The lira continues to recover for the second consecutive session after Qatar announces that it will invest 15 billion dollars in Turkey. Qatar has promised Turkey that it will invest 15 billion dollars in the Turkish economy. This is an aid to the Turkish Government not being forced to resort to the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ). The ruling came out of Wednesday's Aug. 15 meeting between Qatari leader Hamid Bin Al Thani and Turkish President \uc2 Recep Erdogan\uc2 . The two rulers and their finance ministers agreed on this amount of direct investment in Turkey as a buffer against US measures. Numtweet, the spokesman for Ergogan confirmed the amount and assured that the relations between the two countries are based on "true friendship and solidarity." According to Reuters, the money will be channeled to financial markets and Turkish banks. Qatar has pledged $ 15 billion of direct investments in Turkey. Turkish-Qatari relations are based on solid foundations of true frienship and solidarity.\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Ibrahim Kalin\uc2  (@ ikalin1) August 15, 2018 This is one of the responses of the Turkish regime to the advances of the United States that have doubled the rate applied to steel and Turkish aluminum. Previously, Turkey had already decided to boycott technological products and still increase the rate of various goods "made in the USA", namely cars. Bloomberg, \uc2 Mohamed El-Erian\uc2 , economic adviser to Allianz SE, says that this agreement between Qatar and \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  is part of a "strategy to avoid" \uc2 IMF\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, for the analyst, in order for this strategy to be a "sustainable stabilizer", the funds must be larger and have to include the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At this time, interest rates are still low, which is driving up double-digit inflation.\par \par \uc2 The diplomatic dispute with the US led to a steep decline (almost minus 40%) of the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, taking the lira to record lows last Friday. Following the announcement of the investment package, the lira appreciated 7.4%, but is currently up 4.89% to $ 0.165, partially offset by strong losses since Friday. This is the second recovery session.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180815ee8f0043v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
