\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The Mexican peso raises the storm of the Turkish lira\b0\par\par\uc2 756 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY - The Mexican peso gains ground against the dollar on Monday in the midst of economic instability in Turkey and the collapse of the lira. Wholesale, the dollar sells at 19.1636 pesos, or 4% or 80 cents less than the dollar. This Friday's close, according to figures from Bloomberg and the \uc2 Bank of Mexico (Banxico)\uc2 . In bank windows, the dollar sells at 19.20 pesos, that is, five cents less than the close of this Friday, according to the quote of Citibanamex. The purchase is located at 18.40 pesos. Read: The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey\uc2  launches plan to stop the collapse of the lira. According to a report by Banco BASE, although the peso has been affected in the short term, it is an effect of speculative contagion, since there is no strong economic relationship between Mexico and Turkey and an economic crisis in that country that could affect the real economy of some European countries is not imminent.\par \par \uc2  At the beginning of the week, the Turkish lira shows a depreciation of 6.64%, quoting at 6.8295 liras per dollar, after reaching a new historical maximum of 7.23 liras, informed Gabriela Siller, director of Economic-Financial Analysis of Banco BASE. "It should be noted that at its worst level on Monday, the Turkish lira accumulated a depreciation in the year of 90.52%," Siller said in his report. Read: The Turkish lira recovers from a historical low, but the nervousness continues. Central of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the financial system with the aim of ensuring the proper functioning of the markets. Among the measures, there is a reduction in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  requirement that commercial banks must maintain, which implies an injection of liquidity into the market, as well as restrictions on speculative \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Likewise, they do not rule out the possibility of increasing the reference rate, so they will continue to monitor the performance and depth of the market. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision has slowed the fall of the Turkish lira, but it will hardly eliminate speculation against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 , then continue the political frictions between Turkey and the United States, as well as the lack of confidence in the economic policy of the Erdogan government, "said Siller. The analyst also stressed that market participants will remain alert to news about the process of renegotiation of \uc2 NAFTA\uc2 , as the delegation of Mexico will meet again with US officials in Washington. On Friday, Donald Trump said through a tweet that the negotiations between Mexico and the United States are progressing very well, "which in other conditions of the exchange market, probably would have meant an appreciation of the peso," said Siller.MarketsThe Mexican Stock Exchange ( BMV) gains ground after the lows that touched in the previous session, affected like Wall Street by the Turkish lira and the sanctions announced against Turkey. The Price and Quotation Index (S & P / BMV IPC), which groups the 35 most liquid issuers, gains 0.97% to 48,852 units. \uc2 Grupo Financiero Inbursa\uc2  shares lead the gains in the market with an advance of 2.28%; its shares are sold at 30.93 pesos. On Wall Street, the main indices are rising after the announcement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey\uc2 . The \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  industrial index gains 0.13% to 25,346 units, the \uc2 Nasdaq\uc2  has an advance of 0.054% to 7,881 integers and the S & P 500 climbed 0.30% to 2,841 points. Petroleum Oil prices fall on Monday as tension linked to trade conflicts and emerging market problems affected the outlook for fuel demand, although US sanctions against Iran The futures of the West Texas Intermediate (WTI) for delivery in September lost 0.52% to 67.28 dollars per barrel (dpb) while the Brent del MarNorth for delivery in October is sold at 72.65 dpb, which means a drop of 0.22%, according to data from Bloomberg. We recommend: A storm lurks in the oil market thanks to Trump. The Turkish financial crisis raised the risk of contagion in Emerging economies, causing devaluations in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of South Africa, Argentina, Mexico and Russia and pressing their shares, while slowing the growth and the outlook for oil demand, Reuters reported. That adds to nervousness over trade conflicts that are developing between the United States, China and the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , which is feared to lead to a contraction of business activity in the main world economies.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180813ee8d003eq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
