\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-As lira tumbled, Turkey's prime minister won Erdogan over for rate hike\b0\par\par\uc2 830 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2018\par 08:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats story that ran late on Thursday; no change in text)\par \par \uc2 * Lira fell some 20 percent so far this year\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiked top rate after Yildirim \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Erdogan an enemy of interest rates\par \par \uc2 By Orhan Coskun\par \par \uc2 ANKARA, May 25 (Reuters) - It took days of preparation by \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top economic ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the prime minister to convince President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  of the need for a sharp increase in interest rates, three people familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 As a selloff in the lira spiralled toward a full-blown crisis on Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced an emergency increase of its top rate by a 3 percentage points, to 16.5 percent, a move designed to put a floor under Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The decision was the outcome of rounds of talks that started in earnest three days earlier, when Deputy Prime Minister \uc2 Mehmet Simsek\uc2  and Finance Minister Naci Agbal convened an emergency meeting with \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Murat Cetinkaya to address the crisis, the sources said, declining to be identified because of the sensitivity of the information.\par \par \uc2 That the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unable to move immediately, and that its move ultimately required the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Prime Minister \uc2 Binali Yildirim\uc2  two days later, points to tension over monetary policy at the top of Turkey's government.\par \par \uc2 A self-described "enemy of interest rates" Erdogan has, with elections just a month away, repeatedly called for lower borrowing costs to fuel credit growth and spending. International investors want to see higher rates to rein in double-digit inflation and have dumped the lira on concerns about Erdogan's influence over monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 "Was it a late decision? Yes. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not have to trade at these levels if this hike was carried out earlier," said one senior official from Erdogan's ruling AK Party.\par \par \uc2 The ministers believed that it was not just the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at stake - even though the lira had fallen by about a fifth this year - but the need to prevent "permanent damage" to the economy, one of the sources said.\par \par \uc2 They agreed on the need for rate increase to calm the lira, and then conveyed that message to Yildirim, at a separate meeting later on Monday, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 Representatives for Agbal and Simsek could not immediately be reached for comment. No one was immediately available to comment at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the prime minister's office or the presidency.\par \par \uc2 'NOT SO KEEN'\par \par \uc2 More talks followed on Tuesday, where additional potential steps to arrest the lira decline was discussed.\par \par \uc2 Yildirim ultimately broached the topic of a rate hike with Erdogan on Wednesday at their weekly meeting - a full two days after hearing from the ministers about the need for the increase. By then the lira was falling fast, tumbling more than 5 percent at one point.\par \par \uc2 "The need for a rate hike was clearly conveyed," said one of the sources. "Other bureaucrats also took part in the meeting. We know Erdogan was not so keen on this idea."\par \par \uc2 A former transport minister and an Erdogan loyalist, Yildirim's ties to the president date back to the 1990s, when he ran a ferry company in Istanbul, where Erdogan was mayor.\par \par \uc2 He will no longer be prime minister after June, as that position will disappear under a new executive presidency. Instead, he is running for parliament.\par \par \uc2 Much of the lira's selloff was sparked by Erdogan's own comments last week that he expected to assert more monetary policy control after the June 24 parliamentary and presidential elections.\par \par \uc2 The most popular, but also divisive, politician in modern Turkish history, Erdogan has overseen strong economic growth in his 15 years in power but, more recently, also a deepening social crackdown.\par \par \uc2 The rate hike, announced late on Wednesday, was something of a victory for Simsek, a former Wall Street banker seen as one of the most investor-friendly faces in the cabinet.\par \par \uc2 Simsek said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  that it was "high time" that Turkey restored monetary policy credibility, comments that initially helped the lira strengthen.\par \par \uc2 "His tweets were the clearest messages recently. Simsek's statement also boosted the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decisions," said the AKP official.\par \par \uc2 The boost from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move has proved short-lived, with the lira giving up a big slice of the gains on Thursday, as investors bet that more rate hikes will be needed.\par \par \uc2 Since then, the lira has continued to weaken as investors bet that the 3 percentage point increase will not be enough to tame inflation, and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hike again at its next scheduled policy meeting on June 7.\par \par \uc2 "There can be another attack on the lira before (then)...," said the AKP official. "We must be ready for this." (Additional reporting by Ece Toksabay; Writing by David Dolan and Dominic Evans; editing by John Stonestreet) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-5-25T07:43:24.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180525ee5p008wv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
