\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-Turkish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  could raise rates at any time- Erdogan aide\b0\par\par\uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2017\par 12:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Adviser Ertem steps up efforts to boost tumbling lira\par \par \uc2 * Comment at odds with Erdogan's opposition to high rates\par \par \uc2 * But \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has acted in past when lira plummeted\par \par \uc2 * Lira hit by concerns about relations with U.S., deficits\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounds after adviser's comments (Adds quotes, details, background)\par \par \uc2 By Orhan Coskun and Nevzat Devranoglu\par \par \uc2 ANKARA, Nov 23 (Reuters) - \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can raise interest rates at any time, President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 's chief economic adviser said on Thursday, stepping up collective efforts to talk up a local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that an investor selloff has sent tumbling.\par \par \uc2 Erdogan has a long-standing opposition to high interest rates, calling them a tool of exploitation and equating them with treason.\par \par \uc2 But Cemil Ertem told Reuters in an interview the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not hesitate to hike borrowing costs if necessary, including between policy meetings and on top of emergency measures it has already taken this week.\par \par \uc2 The dollar has surged some 17 percent against Turkey's lira since mid-September as foreign investor sentiment towards the country has soured, driven by concerns about frosty relations between Ankara and Washington, twin domestic deficits, and Erdogan's warnings to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "In the case of a deterioration in inflation expectations, the bank can hike rates, and it can do so any time, without necessarily waiting for the (next policy) meeting on Dec. 14," Ertem said.\par \par \uc2 The lira, which fell to a record low of 3.9800 on Wednesday, rebounded after his comments, firming to 3.9045 from 3.9360 beforehand.\par \par \uc2 UNDER PRESSURE\par \par \uc2 Nothwithstanding Erdogan's distaste for high rates, which has raised persistent doubts abroad about the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to act independently of political influence, the bank has moved to hike borrowing costs sharply in the past when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has come under extreme pressure.\par \par \uc2 At an emergency meeting in 2014, it lifted its one-week repo rate from 4.5 percent to 10 percent after an 18 percent rise in the dollar against the lira in little more than a month.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  responded to the current lira selloff with measures to tighten liquidity, reducing commercial banks' borrowing limits on the interbank market for overnight transactions to zero.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Turkey's prime minister and economic czar both tried to bolster the lira, saying the widening rift with the United States was "temporary"..\par \par \uc2 Those strains are focused on the U.S. trial of a Turkish gold trader, \uc2 Reza Zarrab\uc2 , who is accused of violating U.S. sanctions on Iran. Ankara has described the case as a "clear plot against Turkey", and has accused U.S. prosecutors of having links to the cleric it blames for a failed coup last year.\par \par \uc2 Investors, needed by Turkey to cover large budget and current account deficits that a falling lira will make harder still to finance, say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to make a straightforward rate increase rather than just tweaking policy.\par \par \uc2 Ertem said it was wrong to say that measures already taken by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had had no impact, noting the bank had raised the weighted average cost of funding by 25 basis points to 12.25 percent.\par \par \uc2 "You could look and see tomorrow that it raised the late liquidity window (rate)," he added, referring to the highest of several instruments which it uses to set policy. It stands at 12.25 percent.\par \par \uc2 Kapital \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  assistant research manager Enver Erkan, said that, theoretically "a hike of 150-200 basis points in (that)...rate might be necessary."\par \par \uc2 Erdogan, who wants lower rates to boost the economy, said last week a lack of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in policy had left \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  saddled with high inflation.\par \par \uc2 However, Ertem said Erdogan was not targeting the bank's ability to act independently.\par \par \uc2 "The president is not targeting (the bank's) instrument independence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  area. Instrument independence is permanent," he said. (Writing by Daren Butler; Editing by Ece Toksabay and John Stonestreet) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-11-23T12:19:41.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020171123edbn00dto\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
