\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED-UPDATE 2-As lira plumbs record low, Turkey's Simsek says US problems temporary\b0\par\par\uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2017\par 15:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Corrects Haidar Capital Management's assets under management to $365 million from $365 billion in paragraph 11)\par \par \uc2 By Behiye Selin Taner and Daren Butler\par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Nov 22 (Reuters) - Turkish Deputy Prime Minister \uc2 Mehmet Simsek\uc2  on Wednesday attempted to talk up a lira \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has hit record lows for two days running, telling investors that a widening rift with the United States was "temporary".\par \par \uc2 Investors have hammered the lira since September, sending it down some 17 percent on worries about relations with Washington, and nagging concerns about pressure from President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Much of the worry stems from the U.S. trial of Turkish gold trader \uc2 Reza Zarrab\uc2 , who is accused of violating U.S. sanctions on Iran. Ankara has described the case as a "clear plot against Turkey", and has accused the U.S. prosecutors of having links to the cleric it blames for last year's failed coup.\par \par \uc2 "There are serious fluctuations in Turkish markets recently, we need to understand this calmly, correctly and without panicking," Simsek said in a speech in Istanbul.\par \par \uc2 "These are temporary, the problems with the United States and the West are temporary."\par \par \uc2 At 1015 GMT, the lira stood at 3.9624 to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after earlier hitting a new record low of 3.9800.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the \uc2 Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (TCMB) responded to the sell-off with emergency measures to tighten policy, although those have so far failed to shore up confidence. Investors say that, rather than tweaking policy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs a straightforward rate hike.\par \par \uc2 "The TCMB's veiled rate hike yesterday was a step taken to buy time ahead of the Dec. 14 MPC (monetary policy committee) meeting and avoid an interim meeting," said Reel Kapital Securities deputy research manager Enver Erkan.\par \par \uc2 "We do not see this step having a positive impact in the market because it is not a sufficient move," he said. "Hence we expect the negative trend in the lira to continue."\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors, needed by Turkey to finance its large budget and current account deficits, have deep concerns about political pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Erdogan, who wants lower interest rates to fuel lending and construction, said last week a lack of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in policy had left \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  saddled with high inflation.\par \par \uc2 "We're not very positive on Turkey in the near term. Eventually, hopefully enough pressure is brought to bear that they push rates up and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  then does better," said Said Haidar of Haidar Capital Management, a $365 million global macro hedge fund.\par \par \uc2 "It's an ugly looking situation made worse by political issues."\par \par \uc2 The yield on the benchmark 10-year bond rose to 13.08 percent in spot trade on Tuesday from 12.68 percent a day earlier. It dipped to 13.01 percent in Wednesday-dated trade.\par \par \uc2 The main Istanbul share index was up 0.42 percent in early afternoon trade. (Additional reporting by Abhinav Ramnarayan in London; Orhan Coskun and Tuvan Gumrukcu in Ankara; Writing by David Dolan, Editing by William Maclean) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-11-22T15:11:38.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020171122edbm009vl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
