\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-Turkish lira hits record low against dollar on strains in U.S. ties\b0\par\par\uc2 839 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 2017\par 16:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Lira weakens some 17 percent since September\par \par \uc2 * Bond yields up nearly 200 basis points in same period\par \par \uc2 * Deteriorating U.S. ties, monetary policy worries drive losses (Adds Simsek, banks)\par \par \uc2 By Daren Butler and Nevzat Devranoglu\par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Nov 21 (Reuters) - The Turkish lira hit a record low of 3.9780 against the dollar on Tuesday, accelerating losses to some 17 percent since September as concerns widened over Turkey's strained relations with the United States and the independence of its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bank, which is trying to balance the task of containing double-digit inflation with President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 's demands for lower interest rates, responded with emergency measures to tighten policy, although that failed to reverse the slide.\par \par \uc2 The lira's plunge has helped fuel inflation by driving up the cost of energy and other imports. Turkey imports almost all of its energy needs.\par \par \uc2 Worries about U.S. ties centre around the trial of Turkish gold trader \uc2 Reza Zarrab\uc2 , who is accused of violating U.S. sanctions on Iran. The Turkish government spokesman on Monday described the case as a "clear plot against Turkey" that lacks any legal basis.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors, needed by Turkey to finance its large budget and current account deficits, also have deep concerns about political pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Erdogan, who wants lower interest rates to fuel lending and construction, said last week a lack of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in policy had left \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  saddled with high inflation.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. have historically had close ties, but if you look at the events over the past months ... it suggests that relations are deteriorating, and that's certainly a big concern for investors," said William Jackson of \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell as far as 3.9780 to the dollar, eclipsing a previous low of 3.9417 set in January. It was at 3.9575 at 1417 GMT, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's measures. Against the euro, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of some of Turkey's major trading partners, it touched a record low of 4.6711.\par \par \uc2 The lira's slide has been accompanied by a jump of nearly 200 basis points in short-term government debt yields since September, a relatively buoyant period for other emerging markets and global equities.\par \par \uc2 Istanbul's index of banking stocks fell 0.5 percent, underperforming a 0.4 percent rise in the benchmark BIST 100 index, reflecting the concerns about potential fall-out from the Zarrab case.\par \par \uc2 BANKS UNDER PRESSURE\par \par \uc2 U.S. authorities have charged Zarrab, Mehmet Hakan Atilla, an executive at Turkey's state-owned \uc2 Halkbank\uc2 , and seven other alleged co-conspirators with handling hundreds of millions of dollars for Iran's government and Iranian entities from 2010 to 2015, in a scheme to avoid U.S. sanctions.\par \par \uc2 Both Zarrab and Atilla are in U.S. custody and have pleaded not guilty. The trial was due to start in New York on Nov.27, although it has since been delayed by a week.\par \par \uc2 Halkbank\uc2  said all its transactions have fully complied with national and international regulations. Turkey's banking regulator last month dismissed as untrue a local media report alleging banks faced billions of dollars of fines from the United States over Iran sanctions.\par \par \uc2 But investors remain wary. Bank shares have fallen 10 percent since late October, underperforming a 3 percent drop in the benchmark index.\par \par \uc2 Ankara says the Zarrab case is based on fabricated documents. Under a previous investigation that became public in 2013, Turkish prosecutors accused Zarrab and high-ranking Turkish officials of involvement in facilitating Iranian money transfers via gold smuggling, leaked documents at the time showed.\par \par \uc2 Erdogan, then prime minister, cast that investigation as a coup attempt orchestrated by his political enemies. Several prosecutors were removed from the case, police investigators were reassigned, and the investigation was later dropped.\par \par \uc2 Erdogan, who has not been accused of any wrongdoing, has said U.S. prosecutors have shown "ulterior motives" by including references to him and his wife in court papers relating to the trial in New York.\par \par \uc2 BORROWING LIMIT\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would remove banks' borrowing limits on the interbank money market for overnight transactions, and increase their limit for the intraday liquidity facility -- both moves designed to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 An official from the bank said the weighted average cost of funding would be increased to 12.25 percent on Wednesday, up from 11.99 percent on Monday.\par \par \uc2 But Jackson of \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  said such moves fell far short of the outright interest rate increase that markets want to see.\par \par \uc2 "This tweaking at the edges has put the spotlight back onto the fact that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be facing political pressure not to raise interest rates, not to undertake a conventional response to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness," he said.\par \par \