\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Turkey's Erdogan takes aim at  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  independence\b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2017\par 10:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details, background)\par \par \uc2 ANKARA, Nov 17 (Reuters) - Turkish President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  on Friday lashed out at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying a lack of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in monetary policy had left \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  saddled with high inflation and facing a potential slowdown in investment.\par \par \uc2 The comments from Erdogan - some of his starkest yet about the government's need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in policy - immediately weighed on the lira \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "If you try to give loans with such high rates, of course investments will be hindered and halted... We lowered interest rates and inflation fell to single digits," Erdogan told officials from his ruling AK Party in Ankara.\par \par \uc2 "They say, 'The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is independent, so don't interfere'. It is coming to this point because we aren't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The lira \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened to 3.9035 to the dollar following his comments.\par \par \uc2 Erdogan said there may be a meeting next week with the prime minister, relevant ministers and state banks to discuss the issue of high interest rates, Haberturk and other newspapers reported earlier on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "We are determined to deal with the interest rate lobby and interest rates," Haberturk cited Erdogan as telling reporters during a visit to Qatar.\par \par \uc2 Erdogan, an economic populist, wants to see lower interest rates to encourage lending, consumption and construction to boost the economy. He repeated on Friday his oft-stated belief that high interest rates cause inflation - a stance at odds with orthodox economics.\par \par \uc2 His calls for lower interest rates have raised concerns among investors that policy is less than independent in Turkey, hitting the lira \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Reporting by Orhan Coskun and Tuvan Gumrukcu; Writing by David Dolan; Editing by Daren Butler) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-11-17T10:11:41.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020171117edbh00ebg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
