\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Emerging stocks in worst losing streak since May 2016\b0\par\par\uc2 997 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2017\par 11:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 28 (Reuters) - Emerging equities hit one-month lows on Thursday, set for their longest losing streak since May last year, and Turkey's lira and South Africa's rand touched multi-month lows as the dollar and U.S. yields rose.\par \par \uc2 A 0.6 percent fall in MSCI's emerging stocks index extended the benchmark's sell-off into a sixth straight session. The dollar powered to near one-month highs and U.S. 10-year bond yields to near two-month highs.\par \par \uc2 U.S. assets have strengthened after the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  signalled further interest rate rises and on hopes that tax reform proposals from President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will strengthen the economy.\par \par \uc2 Trump has offered to lower corporate income tax rates, cut taxes for small businesses and reduce the top rate for high-earning individuals. Per Hammarlund, chief emerging markets strategist at SEB, said the package was "more aggressive" than the market had anticipated.\par \par \uc2 "The market is over-reacting \u8211\'20\'13 he will have a tough time getting everything through Congress," he said, adding tax reform was as controversial as healthcare reform in the world's largest economy.\par \par \uc2 New orders for key U.S.-made capital goods increased by more than expected in August, strengthening the case for another rate rise before year-end.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong shares were among the biggest laggards, down 0.8 percent, while Taiwan and Russia lost 0.3 percent and South Africa slipped 0.4 percent.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also took a pounding with China's yuan weakening over 0.4 percent to the lowest in more than a month against the dollar, having lost more than 3 percent of its value since hitting a 21-month high in early August.\par \par \uc2 The lira dipped to 2-1/2 month lows before recovering to trade flat, following a vote for independence by the Kurdish population in Iraq that investors fear may inflame separatist tensions in Turkey.\par \par \uc2 Hammarlund said that while the dollar and Treasury yields were the main factors driving down emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the threat of military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a contributing factor for the lira.\par \par \uc2 "That does worry the market as it would be ill-advised for \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 it could really stir domestic violence as well," he said.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's 2030 dollar bond fell another 0.7 cents according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2 , plumbing a 2-1/2 month low, with the 2034 and 2036 issues slipping around 0.5 cents.\par \par \uc2 The rand touched its weakest since mid-May before also rebounding to trade flat. Thousands marched on Wednesday in anti-corruption protests organised by unions.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso hit its lowest since early July, with concerns that \uc2 NAFTA\uc2  trade negotiations could run into 2018, beyond an end-December deadline designed to skirt Mexico's presidential election campaign.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to hold rates at 7 percent at its meeting on Thursday, amid signs that inflation is starting to fall.\par \par \uc2 South Korea's won fell 0.26 percent to a seven-week low, with the government expecting more provocations from North Korea in coming weeks, and the Russian rouble fell 0.2 percent to a one-month low, pressured by an oil price slide.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's forint continued to struggle against the euro in the wake of further monetary easing, weakening 0.2 percent to near five-month lows.\par \par \uc2 In international bond markets, Saudi Arabia completed a $12.5 billion triple-tranche Eurobond sale.\par \par \uc2 Egypt approved a eurobond programme worth around $7 billion for the 2017-2018 fiscal year, state media reported, with the next sale expected before the end of 2017.\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  performance 2017, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2e7eoml"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2e7eoml}}}\uc2  For GRAPHIC on MSCI emerging index performance 2017, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2dZbdP5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2dZbdP5}}}\par \par \uc2 For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par \uc2 For TURKISH market report, see\par \par \uc2 For RUSSIAN market report, see) Emerging Markets Prices from Reuters Equities Latest Net Chg % Chg % Chg\par \par \uc2 on year\par \par \uc2 Morgan Stanley Emrg Mkt Indx 1072.44 -6.13 -0.57 +24.37\par \par \uc2 Czech Rep 1043.68 +1.18 +0.11 +13.25\par \par \uc2 Poland 2437.08 +3.26 +0.13 +25.11\par \par \uc2 Hungary 37415.28 +170.98 +0.46 +16.91\par \par \uc2 Romania 7918.76 +4.52 +0.06 +11.77\par \par \uc2 Greece 756.10 +19.46 +2.64 +17.47\par \par \uc2 Russia 1122.29 -4.65 -0.41 -2.61\par \par \uc2 South Africa 48773.25 -245.00 -0.50 +11.10\par \par \uc2 Turkey 02119.30 +901.01 +0.89 +30.69\par \par \uc2 China 3340.12 -5.16 -0.15 +7.62\par \par \uc2 India 31157.13 -2.68 -0.01 +17.02\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Latest Prev Local Local\par \par \uc2 close \b \highlight22\uc2 currency currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 % change % change\par \par \uc2 in 2017\par \par \uc2 Czech Rep 26.05 26.03 -0.05 +3.69\par \par \uc2 Poland 4.32 4.32 +0.12 +1.99\par \par \uc2 Hungary 311.49 311.23 -0.08 -0.86\par \par \uc2 Romania 4.60 4.60 -0.02 -1.34\par \par \uc2 Serbia 119.35 119.33 -0.02 +3.35\par \par \uc2 Russia 58.26 58.19 -0.13 +5.15\par \par \uc2 Kazakhstan 340.6