\par\par \b \uc2 Turkey - Factors to Watch on July 11\b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2017\par 07:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, July 11 (Reuters) - Here are news, reports and events that may affect Turkish financial markets on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The lira stood at 3.6112 against the U.S. dollar at 0503 GMT, little changed from 3.6080 at Monday's close.\par \par \uc2 The yield on the benchmark 10-year bond was at 10.84 percent in spot trade on Monday and fell to 10.81 percent in Tuesday-dated trade.\par \par \uc2 The main BIST 100 share index rose 1.01 percent to 101,097.16 points on Monday.\par \par \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS\par \par \uc2 Asian shares and the dollar cautiously edged higher on Tuesday, as investors awaited testimony from Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  for clues on when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would tighten U.S. monetary policy. MSCI's broadest index of Asia-Pacific shares outside Japan edged a few points higher in early trading, with sentiment underpinned by technology-led gains on Wall Street.\par \par \uc2 BENCHMARK BOND TAP\par \par \uc2 The Turkish Treasury will tap its benchmark two-year bond maturing on May 15, 2019.\par \par \uc2 WORLD PETROLEUM CONGRESS\par \par \uc2 Oil sector officials and executives will speak at the second full day of the World Petroleum Congress. Turkish Energy Minister Berat Albayrak will hold a news conference (0500 GMT).\par \par \uc2 CYPRUS\par \par \uc2 President of Cyprus \uc2 Nicos Anastasiades\uc2  said on Monday he remained ready to negotiate a peace deal with estranged Turkish Cypriots and Turkey, after \uc2 U.N\uc2 .-backed talks ended in acrimony last week. He said he was still ready to negotiate a deal based on a timetable for the full withdrawal of Turkish troops from the north of the divided island and a commitment from \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it will cease \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Cypriot affairs.\par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on:\par \par \uc2 Turkish politics <TR-POL>\par \par \uc2 Turkish equities <TR-E>\par \par \uc2 Turkish money <TR-M>\par \par \uc2 Turkish debt <TR-D>\par \par \uc2 Turkish hot stocks <TR-HOT>\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  news\par \par \uc2 All emerging market news\par \par \uc2 All Turkish news\par \par \uc2 For real-time quotes, double click on:\par \par \uc2 Istanbul National-100 stock index, interbank lira trading, lira bond trading (Reporting by Daren Butler) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-7-11T06:03:50.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170711ed7b0070v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
