\par\par \b \uc2 Turkey's lira revives as investors look past Fitch downgrade\b0\par\par\uc2 455 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2017\par 13:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ANKARA, Jan 30 (Reuters) - The Turkish lira firmed more than 1 percent on Monday, its biggest percentage advance in six sessions, as investors shrugged off a sovereign debt downgrade by Fitch amid \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts to tighten liquidity.\par \par \uc2 Fitch's downgrade on Friday snuffed out Turkey's last remaining investment grade rating, underscoring deepening concern about politics and monetary policy in what was once a star emerging market.\par \par \uc2 The decision, although widely expected, came hours after rival agency \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  surprised investors by lowering its outlook to "negative" from "stable".\par \par \uc2 "We expect the negative decoupling of the lira to stop unless there is a new, negative development to the contrary," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  liquidity manager at a bank in Istanbul.\par \par \uc2 The lira firmed 1.4 percent against the dollar and was changing hands at 3.8120 at 1131 GMT. Earlier in the session it strengthened as far as 3.7995.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's stock market also advanced, bucking a global trend. The benchmark BIST 100 rose 2.4 percent to 85,814 points.\par \par \uc2 Both Fitch and S&P sounded concern about political insecurity after a failed coup last year, as well as pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . More than 100,000 people have been sacked or suspended in the civil service and the private sector since the abortive July 15 putsch. Thousands more have been arrested.\par \par \uc2 Fitch also cautioned that a looming referendum on reforming the constitution and creating an executive presidency - which is expected in April - would "entrench a system in which checks and balances have been eroded".\par \par \uc2 One of President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 's advisers, Bulent Gedikli, on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  dismissed the Fitch downgrade as "political and not economic" and called it an "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's domestic affairs".\par \par \uc2 Market participants also said the lira was underpinned by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent tightening. The bank this month hiked one of its interest rates by 75 basis points and another by 100, although it kept its benchmark rate on hold.\par \par \uc2 While the increases fell short of investor hopes for sharp rate rises, the bank has also managed to tighten liquidity by closing off some of its funding taps to the market, moves market participants have referred to as "covert tightening".\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weighted average cost of funding spiked to 10.27 percent, its highest in almost three years.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has made a covert rate hike of 200 basis points, and that's not something to be overlooked," said the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  liquidity manager. (Reporting by Nevzat Devranoglu and Ece Toksabay; Writing by David Dolan; Editing by Nick Tattersall and John Stonestreet) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-1-30T13:30:02.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170130ed1u00nme\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
