\par\par \b \uc2 Turkey's Exchange Rate Nears Record Low -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 155 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2015\par 15:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1340 GMT Turkey's real effective exchange rate slumped to 90.85 in September from 95.22 in August, hitting the lowest level since 89.55 in January 2003, when record-keeping started. The measure, which tracks the lira's strength against several other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  adjusted for inflation, has been in steady decline since January. Just two years ago, when the rate was inching toward 120, \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent further appreciation. Now, the lira is hovering near record lows, and the depreciation has stoked inflation toward 8% and hurt consumer confidence. Still, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Erdem Basci refuses to raise interest rates to avoid derailing tepid economic growth. (emre.peker@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 06, 2015 09:40 ET (13:40 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020151006eba6001ny\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
