\par\par \b \uc2 Turkish Lira Tumbles After  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Decisions -- 3rd Update\b0\par\par\uc2 By Yeliz Candemir in Istanbul and Chiara Albanese in London   \par \uc2 849 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2015\par 23:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Turkey's lira sank to record lows on Tuesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest-rates decision and plan to simplify its monetary policy failed to stem deteriorating confidence in the Turkish economy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's moves come amid mounting security threats as Turkey fights a two-front war and collapsing coalition talks that stoke the likelihood of early elections, threatening to further destabilize the country.\par \par \uc2 Members of the bank's Monetary Policy Committee in Ankara said they kept the benchmark one-week repo rate at 7.5% and left the interest-rate corridor unchanged, ranging from the overnight borrowing rate of 7.25% to the 10.75% overnight lending rate.\par \par \uc2 "Taking into account the uncertainty in domestic and global markets and the volatility in energy and food prices, the committee decided to implement a tighter liquidity policy as long as deemed necessary," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said, adding that the lira's weakness is creating inflationary pressure.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after the bank's regular monthly meeting, Governor Erdem Basci unveiled a long-awaited, multipronged road map to simplify his monetary stance by moving toward a single policy rate.\par \par \uc2 Policy makers said the plan will also help combat \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility and safeguard liquidity, highlighting the challenges facing Turkey's economy as the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 's looming interest-rate increase threatens to drain cash from emerging markets that heavily rely on foreign funding.\par \par \uc2 While Turkey's interest-rates decision was in line with eight of the 12 economists' forecasts in a Wall Street Journal survey, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's vaguely stated plan to shift to an orthodox monetary stance fell short of market expectations, fueling the lira rout.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey is making things more toxic, as portfolio bond flows will probably dry up even more," said Luis Costa, emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with \uc2 Citigroup Inc\uc2 . in London.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's lira, this year's worst-performing emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  except Brazil's real, plummeted by more than 1% to a fresh record low of 2.9066 a dollar and to a new all-time low of 3.2098 a euro after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statements.\par \par \uc2 Stocks also took a beating, with the BIST-100 index slumping by 1.25% after trading flat earlier Tuesday. Meanwhile, the government's borrowing costs jumped as benchmark two-year bond yields rose to 10.68% from 10.28%. Bond yields rise as prices drop.\par \par \uc2 "Clearly a case of too little, too late," said Tim Ash, an emerging markets economist at Nomura. "The hope was that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey would get ahead of the curve either with a pre-emptive tightening, or much more hawkish commentary. This does not appear to have been enough."\par \par \uc2 Late Tuesday afternoon, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would also raise the cap on additional daily \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions to $70 million from $30 million, citing "excessive volatility" in exchange rates. The move signals yet another attempt by Mr. Basci to fight lira weakness and financial instability through liquidity \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  instead of interest-rate increases, which would further hamper \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slowing economy.\par \par \uc2 As part of its effort to simplify a complex set of policy tools, Turkish policy makers said they plan to use the benchmark one-week repo rate as an anchor and narrow their interest-rate corridor toward a single rate. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will also boost dollar liquidity to help private borrowers meet foreign debt requirements.\par \par \uc2 "The lira will remain vulnerable as long as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrains from providing the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with concrete support," said \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  analyst Piotr Matys.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's moves follow the failure on Monday of the long-ruling Justice and Development Party's last-ditch effort to form a coalition or minority government.\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Ahmet Davutoglu, who leads an interim government and was tasked with forming Turkey's next administration after elections on June 7 delivered a hung parliament, is poised to give up his mandate to form a government on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  is widely expected to call early elections if the Ankara parliament can't form a coalition by Sunday, the constitutionally mandated deadline.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Turkey's southeast has been rocked by a series of attacks since last month, including a suicide bombing that killed at least 34 people on the Syrian border, assassinations of policemen and daily clashes between Turkish security forces and Kurdish separatists.\par \par \uc2 "Disappointment from politics with no coalition formed yet, and from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  with no simplification of the policy framework, is not great," said Viktor Szabo, who helps oversee $483.3 billion of emerging market debt at \uc2 Aberdeen Asset Management\uc2  in London. "There seems to be little demand to add Turkish risk, as we are now facing another two-to-three months of political uncertainty."\par \par \uc2 Write to Yeliz Candemir at yeliz.candemir@wsj.com and Chiara Albanese at chiara.albanese@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 18, 2015 17:06 ET (21:06 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150818eb8i003ev\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
