\par\par \b \uc2 Turkey's  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Hits New Low -- Barron's Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dimitra DeFotis   \par \uc2 610 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 2015\par 17:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Markets are spooked about the future mix of politics and monetary policy in Turkey, and the lira is dropping to new lows.\par \par \uc2 The iShares MSCI Turkey ETF ( TUR) was down 3% in recent trading. U.S.-traded shares of telecom \uc2 Turkcell\uc2  ( TKC) Akbank ( AKBTY), which reports earnings next week, are each down 1.8%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2 's   Bernd Berg just issued a missive, in which Berg predicts the USD/TRY relationship, having breached 2.70, will fall toward 2.80. He writes: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The Turkish lira is intensifying its rapid decline and is hitting one new all time low after the next over the last trading days. \f28 \uc2 \f2 3M\f28 \uc2 \f2  TRY Vol. has jumped from 14.00% in early April to 16.50% today. Under heavy selling pressure the TRY has breached the 2.70 this morning and is currently trading at 2.7250. In our view the lira is currently the most vulnerable Emerging Market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in an environment of a rising USD due to expected Fed hikes in 2015 and Turkey's reliance on short-term capital inflows that quickly reverse amid the negative external backdrop and weak domestic fundamentals. Political uncertainty and weak domestic fundamentals have been the main trigger for the underperformance of the TRY against its peers in 2015. Especially continuous interference of leading politicians into \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy and disagreements about the right economic strategy to boost growth in Turkey are responsible for the Lira's slide. Today's comments of the government to blame speculators for the lira's slide are just distracting from the rout of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Turkey\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  woes. Any verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the government to stabilize the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is poised to be unsuccessful and investors might continue to withdraw capital from Turkey's markets until the domestic backdrop improves significantly. We therefore expect the Turkish lira to remain under pressure in the weeks ahead."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bloomberg reported early this morning that the lira's double-digit depreciation this year is the most among 24 emerging markets it tracks. The article added:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ruling "AK Party is likely to achieve 42 percent of the vote ... down from 49.8 percent in the 2011 elections. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\f28 \uc2 \f2  has been lobbying for a majority big enough to enable him to alter the constitution to boost the powers of the president's office. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will discuss possible measures "to support the stability in financial markets" at an April 22 meeting on monetary policy, according to a statement on its website on Tuesday."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turkey's bond market is among five that are vulnerable in emerging markets, accoding to Capital Economics. See our post, " Are Some Emerging Market Bonds A Time Bomb?" Also see our post on a \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  study of developing-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reaction to a rise in \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  Yields, " 5 Fragile Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  As Treasury Yields Rise." \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par