\par\par \b \uc2 Turkey's Politics Hit Ratings Outlook -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,534 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 12:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1110 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--\b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's investment-grade status is increasingly threatened by political \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in monetary policy-making, \uc2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\uc2  says. This follows its March survey showed 56% of investors expecting a downgrade to junk by at least one ratings firm in the next two years, up from 44% in February. "Fears of a Turkey ratings downgrade have increased likely in result to political noise around the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  independence," BAML strategists say. The survey includes 54 panelists in Eastern Europe, the Middle East and Africa, with more than $205 billion of assets under management. Turkey is rated BBB- by \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2  and Baa3 by Moody's Investors Service, the lowest rung of investment grade in both agencies, while \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  has the country at BB+, its highest junk rating. (emre.peker@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1103 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The \uc2 State Bank of Vietnam\uc2  said Wednesday it will keep VND/USD exchange rate unchanged despite the market rumors about the possible devaluation of the dong. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply and demand in the local market remain stable. Several analysts have recently said Vietnam should devalue the dong to boost exports, following the strengthening of the greenback. (anhthu.nguyen@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1058 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Myanmar economy will grow at 8.3% in the current fiscal year (ending March 2016), the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asian Development Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  estimates, with growth likely remaining at over 8% in the next fiscal year as well. In a new report, the bank said that this strong growth will be stimulated by an improving business environment and government efforts to reform the once-controlled economy, including tinkering investment laws to make them more friendly to foreign businesses. Inflation, however, will likely accelerate to 8.4% in the 2015 fiscal year, the ADB said, as wages and fiscal spending increases. The country's poorly trained workforce remains a hurdle to economic development, and the ADB says that the Myanmar government must focus on educating and developing the country's youth to prepare them for a modern economy. (shibani.mahtani@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1046 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Even though \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungary's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has resumed its easing cycle, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Concorde Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  continues to see the EUR/HUF below the key 300 mark.Easing between August 2012 and July 2014 weakened the HUF some 7.7% against the EUR.Its revival may have a more muted impact on the exchange rate if, it has any, says economist Janos Samu. Given the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's quantitative easing, the relative stance of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy is less dovish than before, he says. Also, the pickup in Hungary's economic activity is supportive of a stronger exchange rate. Concorde forecasts the EUR/HUF at 298 for end-2014 and 295 for end-2016. EUR/HUF is at 298.97. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 6:44 EDT - The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market since August 2013 through its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -swap auction program, ostensibly to help curtail volatility. But letting that effort expire at month's end might itself prompt less volatility, says Sidnei Nehme of brokerage NGO. He notes the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue rolling over old contracts, which are equivalent to selling dollars in the futures market. Nehme expects dollar to trade at BRL3.1-3.2 this year; it's wrapped up Tuesday at BRL3.125. (rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1043 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2  calculates the ECB's QE program could result in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  buying EUR9 billion of Slovak government bonds. That said, "we estimate there are just EUR9.4 billion bonds by market value that are eligible for these purchases," says Citi's economist Jaromir Sindel, adding the Slovak share of QE-ready bonds is higher than elsewhere in the eurozone. This is due to Slovakia's government debt at 55% of GDP, well below the euro area average 95%, Mr. Sindel says. Also one-third of Slovak debt is either "below 2 years' maturity (or) in foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he says. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  is likely to buy EUR4.7 billion Slovak debt in 2015, amply covering the country's financing needs. (leos.rousek@wsj.com, @LeoRousek) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1037 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The prospects of more rate cuts and expansion of the bond purchases drove Swedish bond yields lower at an auction, while Norway's debt sale benefited from investors' hunt for relatively higher yields, both in strong demand. Sweden sold SEK4 billion, split evenly, in 2019- and 2022-dated debt, with investors continuing to pay to the Swedish state for buying its shorter bond, with the average yield slipping to -0.1666% from -0.1121% previously. Norway sold NOK4 billion of 2025-dated paper, launched two weeks ago, allocating the new tranche at a yield of 1.48%. For comparison: German and Swedish 10-year bond yields trade at 0.22% and 0.39%, respectively. (emese.bartha@wsj; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1030 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungary's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has ensured increased policy flexibility with the widening of its inflation target to a plus or minus 1 percentage point around its re-affirmed 3% inflation goal, Nomura says. Adds inflation will exceed 3% in 1H next year without further government-mandated price cuts, before falling again. Nomura economist Peter Attard Montalto reckons that now the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could technically finish rate cutting only when the CPI forecast was breaching 4%. "That is pushing it somewhat, but it is illustrative of the point that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can cut further to support growth, without been seen as playing too fast and loose with the inflation target." (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1026 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The long-USD squeeze has triggered a painful reversal in the Swiss franc, notes \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2 , with sterling's weakness also a likely contributing factor as some CHF shorts were held versus the pound. The bank says it remains bearish CHF versus both EUR and USD and views current strength as temporary, mainly because the negative Swiss rates make it too painful to hold onto CHF longs. The bank also believes the SNB is likely to act on CHF strength, with a trigger level being close to parity on EUR/CHF. EUR/CHF now at 1.0495, USD/CHF at 0.9580. (gary.stride@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1017 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]-- The U.K. housing market is showing moderate signs of picking up again after cooling down in the final quarter of 2014. Acording to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 British Bankers' Association\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which represents about 200 banks, mortgage deals were on the up in February for the second month in a row, as the economic recovery started feeding into paychecks and interest rates remain low. "We're seeing stronger demand for mortgages as consumers take advantage of some of the very competitive deals currently available," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Richard Woolhouse\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chief economist at the BBA, who underscored consumers are increasingly buying big ticket items. Analysts expect the housing market to continue climbing up at a gradual place during the rest of the year. (jon.sindreu@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1006 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/PHP is higher late Wednesday ahead of the release of U.S. durable goods data and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy meeting on Thursday. A local bank trader said banks have squared their positions ahead of news events. The USD/PHP is at 44.755 after sliding Tuesday to settle at 44.67. Volume is moderate. Traders continue to tip 44.50-45.00 as the near-term trading range for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (cris.larano@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1000 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The next move in U.K. interest rates is likely to be a rise, despite a slowdown in inflation, one of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2 's nine rate-setters says. Minouche Shafik, deputy governor for markets and banking, tells website kentonline.co.uk that inflation is being depressed by temporary factors that will eventually dissipate. Officials' "central expectation" is that their next move will be to raise rates from their historic low of 0.5%, she says. Her remarks contrast with those of BOE Chief Economist \f28 \uc2 \f2 Andrew Haldane\f28 \uc2 \f2 , who said in a recent speech a rate cut was just as likely as a rise. Investors expect the first interest-rate increase in mid-2016. (jason.douglas@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 25, 2015 07:10 ET (11:10 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150325eb3p001cr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
