\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Financial Services News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 603 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2015\par 22:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FINANCIAL SERVICES TOP STORIES \par  \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 MASTERCARD\f28 \uc2 \f2  PROFIT SURGES 29% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MasterCard\f28 \uc2 \f2 's 4Q profit jumped 29% to $801 million, or 69c a share, as the credit-card company posted higher purchase volume and revenue. Shares rose 2% as the results exceeded analysts' expectations. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NYSE GROUP PLANNING MIDDAY AUCTION FOR ITS STOCK MARKETS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 New York Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  is said to be planning to ask regulators for permission to introduce a midday auction as another tool to draw trading away from private venues such as dark pools. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TWO TIGER GLOBAL PARTNERS RESIGN TO START OWN FUNDS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Two partners left $16 billion firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tiger Global Management\f28 \uc2 \f2 , one of the hedge-fund world's marquee names. They are expected to start their own hedge-fund firms, potentially as soon as the end of this year, people familiar with the matter said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GFI SHAREHOLDERS VOTE DOWN $746M SALE TO \f28 \uc2 \f2 CME\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GFI Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  shareholders rejected a buyout proposal from \f28 \uc2 \f2 CME Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and GFI management, according to people familiar with the matter, opening the door for rival \f28 \uc2 \f2 BGC Partners\f28 \uc2 \f2  to press its own hostile bid for the company. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BREVAN HOWARD HEDGE FUND HIT BY OUTFLOWS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors pulled billions of dollars from European hedge fund giant Brevan Howard's flagship fund in the second half of last year, as poor returns pushed the portfolio to its first ever calendar year loss. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  WINS DECURA LAWSUIT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  won a lawsuit brought by Decura IM Investments which alleged that cut backs at the Swiss lender's investment bank meant it had violated the terms of a joint venture. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TURKISH \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO STEM LIRA SLIDE \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Turkey\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  verbally \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the lira's slide as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit record lows against the dollar, seeking to ease fears that policy makers may prematurely cut interest rates despite a broad emerging-markets selloff. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FXCM ADOPTS POISON PILL WITH 10% TRIGGER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FXCM has adopted a shareholder rights plan with a 10% trigger, a move intended to reduce the chance of a hostile takeover attempt at a low valuation. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KCG SWINGS TO PROFIT ON HIGHER TRADING VOLUME \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KCG Holdings swung to a profit in the fourth quarter as market volatility spurred trading volume, especially in equities. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SWISS SNB \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES TOPPED CHF500B AT END OF 2014 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The SNB said its foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  holdings rose 8% to top $539 billion as 2014 drew to a close, raising questions about how the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will manage its considerable reserves after scrapping its cap on the value of the Swiss franc. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MSCI NAMES 3 NEW DIRECTORS, CONCEDING TO VALUEACT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock index provider MSCI appointed three new directors to its board, conceding to activist investor \f28 \uc2 \f2 ValueAct Capital Management\f28 \uc2 \f2 's request for representation. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FRANKLIN RESOURCES\f28 \uc2 \f2  PROFIT FALLS 6.2% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Franklin Resources\f28 \uc2 \f2  said its profit fell 6.2% to $566.4 million as revenue declined 2.1% to $2.06 billion and the firm's assets under management declined from the previous quarter. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BATTLE BREWS OVER BIDS FOR BROKER GFI GROUP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A takeover fight between hard-charging rivals over a broker to Wall Street's biggest banks is coming to a head, a showdown that has split the firm's board amid dueling claims about management conflicts and the hostile bidder's motivations. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LEGG MASON\f28 \uc2 \f2  PROFIT FALLS 5.8% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Legg Mason\f28 \uc2 \f2  earned $77 million, or 67c a share, in the most recent period as revenue declined slightly, but the firm's assets under management grew. It also approved a new share-buyback program for up to $1 billion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 30, 2015 16:00 ET (21:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150130eb1u0048a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
