\par\par \uc2 Top Stories\par \b \uc2 Turkish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Verbally  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  to Stem Lira Slide\b0\par\par\uc2 By YELIZ CANDEMIR   \par \uc2 970 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2015\par 18:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Top North American Financial Services Stories\par \uc2 DJTNAF\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL--\b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the lira's slide as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit record lows against the dollar Friday, seeking to ease fears that policy makers may prematurely cut interest rates despite a broad emerging-markets selloff.\par \par \uc2 Amid sustained pressure on Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday afternoon, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would "use all policy instruments at its disposal" toward meeting inflation targets, hinting that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility may derail anticipated interest-rate reductions.\par \par \uc2 "Recent movements in financial markets are not consistent with the degree of caution of the rate cut cycle envisaged by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Republic of Turkey\uc2 ," policy makers said in a statement shortly before local markets closed.\par \par \uc2 After the \uc2 Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statement, the lira pared losses to as little as 0.5% against both the dollar and the euro. But the impact was short-lived, with the lira 1% weaker against the greenback and down 0.9% versus the euro after markets closed in Istanbul. Meanwhile, benchmark two-year bond yields rose to 6.89% from 6.8% before the statement.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came after a 1.3% drop in the lira to 2.4471 a dollar on Friday, after a surprise rate cut by the \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and contagion fears sent the broadly flat Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbling to yet another all-time low for a second consecutive day.\par \par \uc2 The lira also continued its free fall against the euro, weakening by as much as 1.2% to 2.7699 a euro to its lowest in three weeks despite the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline following the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary-easing decision last week.\par \par \uc2 Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Erdem Basci's suggestion on Tuesday that policy makers may convene an emergency meeting on Feb. 4 to cut interest rates has been fueling the lira selloff, now in its sixth day. While some analysts interpreted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Friday statement as a sign that the governor wouldn't convene an extraordinary meeting, the communique and a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman didn't explicitly rule out the option.\par \par \uc2 "We were quite doubtful about the viability of the meeting, having seen the sharp depreciation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; although we were thinking that political pressure may urge the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey to go for it," said Ozlem Derici, chief economist at Deniz Invest in Istanbul. "It seems that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will wait for the original date of the meeting on February 24th and follow market conditions to better assess whether it is the right time to ease monetary policy."\par \par \uc2 The lira's slide started in early December, amid signs that the economic recovery in the U.S. would prompt the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  to start raising interest rates in a move that threatens to suck money out of emerging markets like Turkey. The sell-off accelerated in mid-January, driven by mounting political pressure on \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut interest rates. The lira has slumped 4.4% against the greenback since the beginning of this year and lost nearly 4% since Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The government and President \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  have been pressuring the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily for the past month, saying significant cuts to borrowing costs are needed to stimulate growth in Turkey's slowing $820 billion economy.\par \par \uc2 "Recently signaled emergency rate cuts were anyway beginning to--mildly--pressure the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Tatha Ghose and Simon Quijano-Evans, London-based \uc2 Commerzbank AG\uc2  analysts. "The situation worsened because of a general risk-off tone around the region, perhaps driven by concern surrounding Russia."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Basci said this week that Turkey's inflation rate is poised to slow rapidly in January, justifying reductions to interest rates. Consumer-prices will increase by an annualized 6.8% in January, according to a survey of seven economists by The Wall Street Journal, down from 8.17% in December.\par \par \uc2 Before Friday's verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , many economists--including from \uc2 J.P. Morgan Chase & Co\uc2 . and \uc2 Citigroup Inc\uc2 .--had said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on track to cut its policy rate to 7% from 7.75% next week. Mr. Basci had said policy makers may hold an extraordinary meeting to reduce borrowing costs Wednesday if official data Tuesday shows that inflation slowed by more than 1 percentage point in January.\par \par \uc2 A fresh drop in one-week repo rate would mark the second reduction following a 0.5 percentage point decrease from 8.25% on Jan. 20, when Mr. Basci resumed a monetary policy easing cycle he had halted for five months.\par \par \uc2 Some government ministers and the president slammed the last decision as "insufficient" to incentivize investments and support tepid economic growth--about 3% last year. On Friday, Economy Minister Nihat Zeybekci dismissed concerns about the lira's free fall, saying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation should not stand in the way of lower interest rates.\par \par \uc2 "At the present juncture, interest-rate reductions are already late," Mr. Zeybekci said as the lira slumped to fresh lows against the dollar. "We find it meaningless for Turkey to tolerate high interest rates by acting with apprehension."\par \par \uc2 Emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under renewed pressure after \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced its one-week repo rate to 15% from 17%, surprising markets and causing investors to shun risky assets--including Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The lira will remain vulnerable as long as investors perceive that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is submitting to political pressure to cut rates," said Paul McNamara, an emerging-markets bond investor who oversees about $5 billion at GAM, an asset-management firm. "With significant, mostly private foreign debt, loose monetary policy--especially anything that makes effective interest rates close to inflation--poses a significant risk to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Write to Yeliz Candemir at yeliz.candemir@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJTNAF1120150130eb1u0001b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
