\par\par \b \uc2 VLE Valeura sells 1,306 boe/d in Q1\b0\par\par\uc2 Stockwatch   \par \uc2 916 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2014\par \uc2 Canada Stockwatch\par \uc2 CNSW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Canjex Publishing Ltd.   \par \par \uc2 Valeura Energy Inc\uc2  (2) (TSX:VLE)\par \par \uc2 Shares Issued 57,906,135\par \par \uc2 Last Close 4/9/2014 $0.67\par \par \uc2 Wednesday April 09 2014 - News Release\par \par \uc2 Mr. Jim McFarland\uc2  reports\par \par \uc2 VALEURA PROVIDES FIRST QUARTER 2014 \b \highlight22\uc2 OPERATIONAL\b0 \highlight\uc2  UPDATE\par \par \uc2 Valeura Energy Inc\uc2 . has provided an \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  update for the first quarter of 2014.\par \par \uc2 Net sales up 10 per cent in the first quarter of 2014 and tracking guidance\par \par \uc2 Net corporate petroleum and natural gas sales in the first quarter of 2014 averaged approximately 1,306 barrels of oil equivalent per day, up 10 per cent from the fourth quarter of 2013 reflecting the contribution from two new horizontal wells completed with multistage fracs, frac completions on two vertical wells drilled in 2013 and six shallow gas well recompletions in the Thrace basin of Turkey. This is the third consecutive quarter of increasing net sales.\par \par \uc2 Net sales in Turkey in the first quarter of 2014 averaged 1,274 barrels of oil equivalent per day, including 7.6 million cubic feet per day of natural gas at an average wellhead price of $9.64 per thousand cubic feet and seven barrels of oil per day. Net sales in Canada averaged 32 barrels of oil equivalent per day.\par \par \uc2 First quarter 2014 net sales are tracking 2014 annual guidance, which targets 5- to 10-per-cent annualized growth from fourth quarter 2013 sales (1,250- to 1,310-barrel-of-oil-equivalent-per-day average sales in 2014) based on a self-financed capital expenditure program of $14-million to $17-million (net).\par \par \uc2 The average wellhead price realization in Turkey of $9.64 per thousand cubic feet in the first quarter of 2014 was down 3 per cent from the fourth quarter of 2013 reflecting some further weakening in the Turkish lira, which is the pricing basis for Turkish gas sales. In the fourth quarter of 2013, the average Canadian-dollar to Turkish-lira exchange rate was 1.93. The exchange rate subsequently peaked in January, 2014, at 2.10 before \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Jan. 28, 2014, to stabilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by lifting interest rates. In the first quarter of 2014, the Canadian-dollar/Turkish-lira exchange rate averaged 2.00. The Turkish lira has further strengthened to the current Canadian-dollar/Turkish-lira exchange rate of approximately 1.92 following the results of the March 30 local elections in Turkey, in which the ruling AK party received the strongest support, winning more than 43 per cent of the popular vote.\par \par \uc2 Thrace basin \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  highlights\par \par \uc2 The corporation drilled and fracked two new horizontal wells, BTD-2H and TDR-11H, in the Tekirdag area on joint venture lands acquired from Thrace Basin Natural Gas (Turkiye) Corp. and Pinnacle Turkey Inc. (Valeura 40 per cent). These wells are the fourth and fifth horizontal wells drilled in the TBNG JV and the first horizontal wells drilled into the Mezardere formation, building on the success of an earlier 17-well re-entry frac program in this formation in existing wells. Drilling times and costs for the BTD-2H and TDR-11H wells showed continued improvement from earlier horizontal wells and bettered budget estimates.\par \par \uc2 The BTD-2H well was drilled in 13 days to a vertical depth of 635 metres into the Mezardere formation with a horizontal section of 476 metres and was subsequently completed with an eight-stage frac on March 4. The well is tied into the gathering system and, over the initial 30 days since tie-in, flowed at an average rate of 1.5 million cubic feet per day (gross) through a range of choke sizes from 28/64ths of an inch to 42/64ths of an inch. The well has recovered all of the completion load fluid and is currently flowing at a restricted rate of approximately 2.3 million cubic feet per day through a 42/64th-of-an-inch choke. (Note that the initial production rates stated throughout this press release are not necessarily indicative of long-term performance or ultimate recovery and are subject to decline rates.)\par \par \uc2 The TDR-11H well was drilled in 11 days to a vertical depth of 518 metres into the Mezardere formation with a horizontal section of 678 metres and was subsequently completed with a 10-stage frac on March 25. The well is tied into the gathering system and flowed at an initial restricted rate of approximately two million cubic feet per day (gross) through a 32/64th-of-an-inch choke. The well is continuing to clean up with approximately 45 per cent of the completion load fluid recovered to date.\par \par \uc2 The final costs to drill, frac and tie in the BTD-2H and TDR-11H wells were approximately $2.4-million and $2.7-million (gross), respectively. These costs are below the corporation's budgeted average cost of $3.0-million (gross) per well.\par \par \uc2 Outlook\par \par \uc2 The corporation has budgeted up to 10 additional drill wells in 2014, including up to six horizontal or vertical wells into the Mezardere and Teslimkoy formations in the Tekirdag area, targeting tight gas, and up to four vertical wells, targeting conventional shallow gas, likely in the Osmanli area on new 3-D seismic acquired in the fourth quarter of 2013.\par \par \uc2 The well re-entry frac program of up to 13 wells and the shallow gas recompletion program are expected to continue at a relatively steady pace through the rest of 2014.\par \par \uc2 We seek Safe Harbor.\par \par \uc2 Dokument CNSW000020140409ea49009hp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
