\par\par \b \uc2 Turkish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  to Meet on Lira Concerns\b0\par\par\uc2 By Yeliz Candemir   \par \uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2014\par 13:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL--The Turkish lira rebounded strongly Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would schedule an extraordinary policy meeting on Tuesday to evaluate recent developments and take necessary measures to ensure price stability.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the decision would be published midnight local time (2200 GMT) on Tuesday. The news appeared to be interpret as a signal that Ankara would raise interest rates aggressively, sending the lira 2% higher at 1100 GMT.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said that failure to deliver significant increase in interest rates could spark a broad selloff. "They have to hike...and aggressively, " said Tim Ash, emerging markets economist at Standard Bank in London.\par \par \uc2 The news comes after the lira has endured its sharpest monthly decline for more than five years as investors have dumped the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on broad concerns over emerging markets and specific concerns over political risk in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first time in two years in an attempt to shore up the lira by spending precious foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 Turkish markets have been hit hard by the U.S. Federal Reserve's tapering plans and by local political tensions. A corruption probe launched Dec. 17 has targeted Prime Minister \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 's allies, forced a cabinet reshuffle, further fueled the lira selloff and sent borrowing costs surging.\par \par \uc2 Write to Yeliz Candemir at yeliz.candemir@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 27-01-14 1238GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020140127ea1r0008y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
