\par\par \b \uc2 Turkey's lira plummets to record low as emerging markets retreat\b0\par\par\uc2 183 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2014\par 17:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Jan 24 (Reuters) - Turkey's lira touched a record low against the dollar on Friday, amid a sell-off in emerging markets, just a day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to halt its slide.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lira slid as far as 2.3360 against the dollar, from 2.3050 late on Thursday. By 1545 GMT, it was at 2.3275.\par \par \uc2 The lira has fallen 10 percent against the dollar over the past month, pulled down by a corruption scandal and by the winding down of U.S. monetary stimulus. Investors had been crying out for a rate hike to defend it.\par \par \uc2 With no trades recorded in the afternoon, the yield on the 10-year benchmark bond rose to 10.44 percent from 10.37 percent a day earlier.\par \par \uc2 The main Istanbul stock index closed down 1.53 percent at 64,427.52 points, in line with the main global emerging market index. (Reporting by Dasha Afanasieva; Editing by Larry King)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-1-27T16:17:01.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140124ea1o00ayq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
