\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ.com What's News - Worldwide News Briefs For Jan 23\b0\par\par\uc2 811 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2014\par 19:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S., SYRIA SPAR AT PEACE CONFERENCE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Secretary of State John Kerry kicked off talks aimed at ending the Syrian civil war by demanding the removal of President Bashar al-Assad from power. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WEST EXPLORES PLAN B FOR FORCES IN AFGHANISTAN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Senior Western officials have concluded that Afghan President Hamid Karzai won't sign a security deal with the U.S., and they are exploring other ways to retain foreign forces in the country after the coalition's mandate expires in December. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI PROTEST LEADER DEFIES EDICT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thai antigovernment protest leader Suthep Thaugsuban took to the streets, defying the declaration of a state of emergency and collecting more funds from demonstrators. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAX OVERHAUL PROCEEDING ON SCHEDULE: OECD \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An overhaul of international taxation designed to eliminate loopholes that enable many companies to keep their tax bills low is proceeding on schedule, the OECD said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CANADIAN REGULATORS URGE TOUGHER STANDARDS FOLLOWING RAIL DISASTER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canadian regulators said Canada should immediately implement enhanced safety measures for railcars that carry dangerous goods. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MANUFACTURING ACTIVITY SLIPS IN CHINA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A closely watched gauge of China's manufacturing output slipped to a six-month low, indicating a contraction in manufacturing activity in the world's second-largest economy. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINESE DEFICIT BELOW FORECAST \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's fiscal gap for 2013 fell short of the government's budget projections, reflecting less aggressive spending on some social programs and better-than-expected revenue despite slower economic growth. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 3 DEAD, 30 MISSING IN QUEBEC FIRE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Quebec police said three people were confirmed dead and another 30 were missing after an early-morning fire broke out in a seniors' residence in a small Quebec hamlet. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RUSSIAN COURT ORDERS LEBEDEV'S RELEASE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The country's supreme court ordered that former Yukos oil tycoon Mikhail Khodorkovsky's jailed business partner, Platon Lebedev, be freed, bringing an end to the country's highest profile criminal case. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BERLUSCONI UNDER INVESTIGATION FOR ALLEGED WITNESS-TAMPERING \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Former Italian Premier Silvio Berlusconi is under investigation for alleged witness-tampering during a trial last year that saw him sentenced to seven years in jail for having sex with an underage prostitute and abuse of office. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRENCH ECONOMIC DATA DISAPPOINT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 France's economic activity contracted for third straight month in January as President Fran\u231\'00\'E7ois Hollande reaches out to business to spark growth. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EURO-ZONE BUSINESS ACTIVITY PICKS UP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro-zone economy started the year on a stronger note, with Germany leading a January pickup in business activity, while consumers were more optimistic than at any time since June 2011. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 TURKEY INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO HALT LIRA SLIDE \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Turkey\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets for the first time in two years in an effort to slow the lira's free fall. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPAIN JOB MARKET SHOWS SIGN OF TURN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spain posted seasonally adjusted job growth for the first time in nearly six years, a potential turning point for one of Europe's most depressed labor markets. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MANTEGA SEES BRAZIL POISED FOR GROWTH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's economy is poised for acceleration from recent disappointing growth rates amid a still gradual global recovery, Finance Minister Guido Mantega said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STRIKE HITS SOUTH AFRICA PLATINUM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tens of thousands of platinum workers went on strike to demand higher salaries, bringing a key part of South Africa's economy to a near standstill. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HONG KONG TO DESTROY IVORY STOCKPILE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's government said it would destroy its 30-ton stockpile of seized elephant ivory, one of the largest in the world, following similar moves in the U.S. and China. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KIDNAPPED KOREAN OFFICIAL RESCUED \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A South Korean trade agency official has been released unharmed after three days of being held hostage by gunmen in Libya, the foreign ministry in Seoul said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PAKISTAN HIT BY NEW MILITANT ATTACKS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pakistan's Islamist militants continued their blitz of attacks Wednesday, as the government came under intense pressure to make clear its counterterrorism policy. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TEXAS EXECUTES MEXICAN DESPITE DIPLOMATIC PROTESTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Texas executed a Mexican man despite strong objections from the Mexican government and U.S. diplomats that it would violate international law. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ STICKS TO UPBEAT VIEW \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  sticks to its bullish view on inflation and the economy, dashing market expectations for imminent fresh action. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BULGARIA FACES CRITICISM OVER NEW CRIME BILL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The controversial new bill could see the former Eastern bloc member clash with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  over human rights. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ISRAEL SAYS IT FOILED AL QAEDA PLOT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Israel on Wednesday said it arrested three Palestinians that it alleged were part of al Qaeda-inspired group plotting a suicide bombing of the U.S. Embassy in Tel Aviv, along with other attacks in Israel and the West Bank.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (For continuously updated news from the Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 \f2 .)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 23, 2014 13:01 ET (18:01 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140123ea1n002v7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
