\par\par \b \uc2 Turkish  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fails to Stem Lira Sell-Off\b0\par\par\uc2 1,006 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2014\par 18:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL--\b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resorted Thursday to direct \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales for the first time in two years to prop up the lira, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept on spiraling to record lows amid a broad-based investor exodus from emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 Policy makers in Ankara started selling dollars in the European morning as the dollar jumped to 2.2973 against the lira, according to traders familiar with the transaction. The lira bounced back somewhat in response, but plunged again within hours. That drew in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a second time, traders said, but again the lira quickly sank, with the dollar soaring above 2.30 to the lira.\par \par \uc2 Mounting expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve will increase the rate at which its scaling back monthly bond purchases has hit economies dependent on international investors to plug external funding shortfalls, such as Turkey and South Africa. The pressure also spread to other developing nations like Argentina, which faces rising inflation and social unrest, as well as Russia and Mexico.\par \par \uc2 "It's been a concerted selloff in emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a day of big losses for the high-yielding pack across the board. Turkey is the classic example. Current account is still huge and we have political layers," said Luis Costa, a \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  strategist in London. "The story in the lira is extremely complicated and at 2.3 is has much further to go. We are short of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The move has been way too fast and has broken all forecasts."\par \par \uc2 In a one-sentence emailed statement after the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was taking this action because of "unhealthy price developments." A spokesman declined further comment and the policy makers haven't provided an update.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has wasted precious \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves today on what was--and would always be in the absence of meaningful rate hikes--a futile \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  effort," said Peter Kinsella, senior foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  in London. "The move higher shows no signs of stopping and unless we see aggressive countermeasures from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there could be a more aggressive run on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming weeks."\par \par \uc2 Turkish markets have been hit hard by the Fed's tapering plans and by local political tensions. A corruption probe launched Dec. 17 has targeted Prime Minister Recep Tayyip Erdogan's allies, forced a cabinet shuffle, further fueled the lira selloff, and sent borrowing costs soaring.\par \par \uc2 One easy, though not risk-free fix would be to raise interest rates. But on Tuesday, Governor Erdem Basci budged an outright bump to his key policy rates, instead introducing a new lending tool that economists said amounted to a backdoor rate hike. Mr. Erdogan has repeatedly blamed a so-called interest-rate lobby of economists, investors and journalists of seeking to destabilize Turkey and its markets for their own profit.\par \par \uc2 "It appears that political pressure has been brought to bear on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  not to hike rates. Markets did not react well, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to step up its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman & Co\uc2 . strategists led by Marc Chandler in New York.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 , which has recently criticized \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for its opaque monetary policies, urged policy makers to stick to a flexible exchange rate and argued that an interest-rate increase should be the immediate priority to tame near-rampant inflation. Turkey saw price increases of 7.4% in 2013, compared with its 5% official target.\par \par \uc2 "What matters is that monetary policy avoids second-round effects to inflation by ensuring a strong nominal anchor," IMF spokesman William Murray said.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's lira is in its longest losing streak since August 2001, which had triggered an economic crisis and caused the banking system to collapse. Still, the country is at a much stronger financial position now: the government sold a $2.5 billion bond Wednesday that was four times oversubscribed, the Treasury said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 But the lira's future direction largely depends on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to persuade investors that it will use its new extraordinary days of additional monetary tightening, which Mr. Basci says will effectively raise borrowing costs. Monday is poised to be the first such day, followed by Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "The market sent a very clear message to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  today: it wants monetary tightening. The remedy is in long-term extraordinary days, otherwise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales will not be effective," said Murat Yardimci, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at ING Bank in Istanbul.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a lot more aggressive in the past, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is actually strong but markets find the national lender's stance weak," said Ozlem Derici, chief economist at Deniz Invest in Istanbul. "The markets still lack trust in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I expect it to continue its direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Policy makers have already burned through at least $19 billion, a third of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's net reserves, in an unsuccessful effort to halt the lira's slide since last June. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined 21% against the dollar last year, making it one of the worst performers in emerging markets and a leading loser among developing economies with a 7% drop this year.\par \par \uc2 "Rule number one of direct \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when you \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , do it in massive size and make sure it is effective. I guess the message from today's move is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey just did not do enough," said Tim Ash at Standard Bank in London. "The cover for \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is that we are seeing broader-based emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness, including the ruble and the South African rand, which makes the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  more difficult to understand."\par \par \uc2 Chiara Albanese and Ian Talley contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Emre Peker at emre.peker@wsj.com and Yeliz Candemir at yeliz.candemir@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 23, 2014 12:20 ET (17:20 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN0000201401